  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The essay stresses that a repository rarely captures the full behavior of a legacy service: contracts, migrations, user journeys and institutional knowledge remain external. Small reversible changes, context gathering and reproducible tests are offered as controls against locally successful but architecturally wrong agent patches.</data>
  <data key="d264">Reliable agents in mature codebases need recovered tacit constraints and regression evidence before modifying code.</data>
  <data key="d265">Inventory external invariants and dependencies before delegation; Make brownfield changes incremental and reversible; Verify old behavior alongside new acceptance criteria.</data>
