  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/human-judgment-doesnt-leave-the-software</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-08-21</data>
  <data key="d79">Agentic factories relocate human responsibility toward intent, quality criteria and authorization rather than eliminating it.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Put human judgment at the intention and acceptance boundaries; Automate early regression and security checks; Escalate design ambiguity and irreversible operations to authorized owners.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The article compares human-supervised and largely unattended factories and asks who defines product intent, architectural trade-offs and unacceptable regressions. It advocates persistent checks, managed risk boundaries and explicit ownership even when many implementation steps run without a person present.</data>
  <data key="d264">Agentic factories relocate human responsibility toward intent, quality criteria and authorization rather than eliminating it.</data>
  <data key="d265">Put human judgment at the intention and acceptance boundaries; Automate early regression and security checks; Escalate design ambiguity and irreversible operations to authorized owners.</data>
