<node id="O008">
  <data key="d73">Software Factories, Light and Dark</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d76">2026</data>
  <data key="d77">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d78">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/software-factories-light-and-dark</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-07-22</data>
  <data key="d79">A software factory is many governed loops; its level of human involvement changes both risk and total operating cost.</data>
  <data key="d80">A conceptual taxonomy and projections, not a controlled comparison of factory operating models.</data>
  <data key="d81">Separate an autonomous loop from the governance system supervising many loops; Measure cost of failures and rework, not just generation speed; Choose review intensity by reversibility and blast radius.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The essay contrasts "light" factories that retain human interpretation with "dark" factories that minimize review, exposing the trade-off between throughput and lost comprehension. Osmani argues that harness capability and measurable verification should determine safe autonomy, not the attraction of unattended execution.</data>
  <data key="d264">A software factory is many governed loops; its level of human involvement changes both risk and total operating cost.</data>
  <data key="d265">Separate an autonomous loop from the governance system supervising many loops; Measure cost of failures and rework, not just generation speed; Choose review intensity by reversibility and blast radius.</data>
