  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/own-the-outer-loop</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/own-the-outer-loop</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-07-09</data>
  <data key="d79">Engineers can delegate the inner execution loop while retaining ownership of quality criteria, verdicts and consequences.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Define quality signals before execution; Separate the checker from the final acceptance authority; Require a named owner with authority to stop or roll back.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">Osmani distinguishes producing code and testing artifacts from accepting the evidence those checks produce. He locates professional accountability in the surrounding outer loop: intent, checks, risk appetite, provenance, approval and action if a released change fails.</data>
  <data key="d264">Engineers can delegate the inner execution loop while retaining ownership of quality criteria, verdicts and consequences.</data>
  <data key="d265">Define quality signals before execution; Separate the checker from the final acceptance authority; Require a named owner with authority to stop or roll back.</data>
