  <data key="d273">true</data>
  <data key="d274">2026-10-10</data>
  <data key="d275">comparison/analogy, not observed citation, causal validation or replication</data>
  <data key="d276">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence. Framework or market hypothesis is an authored practitioner proposal, not an empirically validated scale or intervention.</data>
  <data key="d277">W192 is a data-resource study, not independent validation of a two-axis autonomy framework; W152 is a better research-roadmap comparator.; The original essay explicitly introduces two dimensions (agency and orchestration) and six levels; the earlier one-dimensional paraphrase dropped the framework.; Represent the genuine two-axis framework and its six levels rather than reducing it to a generic risk-tier recommendation.; Capture the two axes, scope of six levels, and lack of empirical validation.; Agency vs orchestration is best represented through execution, human-agent delegation and escalation.; Do not promote conceptual taxonomy or market hypotheses into established research outcomes.</data>
