<node id="O013">
  <data key="d73">Long-running Agents</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">System knowledge &amp; memory</data>
  <data key="d76">2026</data>
  <data key="d77">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d78">https://addyo.substack.com/p/long-running-agents</data>
  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/long-running-agents</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/long-running-agents</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-04-30</data>
  <data key="d79">Agents operating across sessions require durable task state, resumability, recovery and verifiable progress.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Persist decisions and current state outside the transient model context; Make retries idempotent and restartable; Verify continuity and completion against external artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The article examines context-window exhaustion, repeated mistakes and premature "done" claims in workflows lasting days. It recommends structured progress artifacts, checkpoints, clean workspaces and independent acceptance tests to support handoffs between agent sessions.</data>
  <data key="d264">Agents operating across sessions require durable task state, resumability, recovery and verifiable progress.</data>
  <data key="d265">Persist decisions and current state outside the transient model context; Make retries idempotent and restartable; Verify continuity and completion against external artifacts.</data>
