  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/14-more-lessons-from-14-years-at</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-02-12</data>
  <data key="d79">Long-lived engineering teams depend on trust, clear decision-making, effective communication and organizational stewardship.</data>
  <data key="d80">Personal career retrospective; no original AI-specific field experiment.</data>
  <data key="d81">Make decision rights and handoffs visible; Value team reliability above heroic individual throughput; Use as background principles, not an AI impact study.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">B</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">A second retrospective about long-term team effectiveness stresses the structures around projects: communication, ownership, priorities, collaboration and shared decisions. These lessons provide organizational context rather than new research on AI agents.</data>
  <data key="d264">Long-lived engineering teams depend on trust, clear decision-making, effective communication and organizational stewardship.</data>
  <data key="d265">Make decision rights and handoffs visible; Value team reliability above heroic individual throughput; Use as background principles, not an AI impact study.</data>
