<node id="O018">
  <data key="d73">How to write a good spec for AI agents</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d76">2026</data>
  <data key="d77">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d78">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-to-write-a-good-spec-for-ai-agents</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-01-19</data>
  <data key="d79">A useful agent specification is compact, testable and iterative rather than a giant prompt resembling an unvalidated requirements dump.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Specify desired behavior and forbidden regressions separately from implementation detail; Plan before writes, then build in small independently checked increments; Update specification when evidence reveals an ambiguity.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">Osmani provides guidance on the degree of detail in requirements, decomposition into small tasks, read-only planning and successive execution. Intent, constraints, expected behavior and testing guidance become checkpoints throughout development.</data>
  <data key="d264">A useful agent specification is compact, testable and iterative rather than a giant prompt resembling an unvalidated requirements dump.</data>
  <data key="d265">Specify desired behavior and forbidden regressions separately from implementation detail; Plan before writes, then build in small independently checked increments; Update specification when evidence reveals an ambiguity.</data>
  <data key="d84">2026</data>
  <data key="d92">4.1</data>
