<node id="O019">
  <data key="d73">Code Review in the Age of AI</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d76">2026</data>
  <data key="d77">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d78">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/code-review-in-the-age-of-ai</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-01-05</data>
  <data key="d79">The rise in generated changes makes code review an explicit burden-of-proof and accountability process.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Attach objective verification artifacts to pull requests; Review intent, integration risk and sensitive paths; Never treat a passing self-generated test as independent approval.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The essay argues that tests, reproducible manual checks and a stated risk assessment should accompany every proposal. Teams should preserve contextual knowledge and ownership rather than confusing a model-generated diff with evidence that the resulting change is safe.</data>
  <data key="d264">The rise in generated changes makes code review an explicit burden-of-proof and accountability process.</data>
  <data key="d265">Attach objective verification artifacts to pull requests; Review intent, integration risk and sensitive paths; Never treat a passing self-generated test as independent approval.</data>
  <data key="d84">2026</data>
  <data key="d92">8.9</data>
