<node id="O020">
  <data key="d73">How Good Is AI at Coding React (Really)?</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d76">2025</data>
  <data key="d77">Addy Osmani</data>
  <data key="d78">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-good-is-ai-at-coding-react-really</data>
  <data key="d168">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-good-is-ai-at-coding-react-really</data>
  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/how-good-is-ai-at-coding-react-really</data>
  <data key="d173">2025-12-29</data>
  <data key="d79">React-related AI success is highly task-dependent, with integration and usability much harder to establish than component scaffolding.</data>
  <data key="d80">Numerical benchmark claims are a synthesis of separate benchmarks with different tasks, versions and measurement methods; not directly comparable.</data>
  <data key="d81">Benchmark scores have task- and version-specific denominators; Use browser tests and accessibility review for end-to-end UI changes; Treat reported percentages as third-party snapshot results, not the author’s experimental measurement.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">B</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">Using third-party web and coding benchmarks, Osmani contrasts relatively tractable isolated UI tasks with weaker multi-step integration. He recommends context-rich specifications, UI standards, accessibility checks and browser-level evaluation instead of equating code generation with product quality.</data>
  <data key="d264">React-related AI success is highly task-dependent, with integration and usability much harder to establish than component scaffolding.</data>
  <data key="d265">Benchmark scores have task- and version-specific denominators; Use browser tests and accessibility review for end-to-end UI changes; Treat reported percentages as third-party snapshot results, not the author’s experimental measurement.</data>
  <data key="d84">2025</data>
  <data key="d92">3.4</data>
  <data key="d266">C03</data>
  <data key="d267">Direct</data>
  <data key="d94">curated practitioner article (not a research study)</data>
  <data key="d268">false</data>
  <data key="d269">W191;W193;W111</data>
  <data key="d95">Osmani public Substack sitemaps 2024/2025/2026 plus individual source URLs; independent editorial review 2026-10-10</data>
  <data key="d97">Overlay only; does not change any original W001-W193 evidence classification</data>
  <data key="d270">Numerical benchmark claims are a synthesis of separate benchmarks with different tasks, versions and measurement methods; not directly comparable. Any externally quoted benchmark, productivity or vendor telemetry requires independent verification of original method and population.</data>
  <data key="d271">yes</data>
  <data key="d90">https://addyo.substack.com/sitemap/2025</data>
