  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">This earlier essay stresses reading AI code closely so that humans connect implementation back to intent, testing and maintenance. Its strong line-by-line reading prescription is explicitly revised in the September 2026 "The Code Nobody Reads" essay, which advocates risk-tiered independent checking.</data>
  <data key="d264">AI-generated code should be treated as an untrusted draft and not merged without responsible understanding and verification.</data>
  <data key="d265">Verify AI output against requirements before acceptance; Record decision ownership; Document the change in the author’s proposed review policy over time.</data>
