  <data key="d173">2025-08-30</data>
  <data key="d79">Fast conversational prototyping and accountable AI-assisted engineering are distinct development regimes.</data>
  <data key="d80">Practitioner interpretation; not primary experimental evidence.</data>
  <data key="d81">Choose rigor appropriate to the target environment; Require explicit acceptance contracts for production work; Teach the transition from prototype to maintainable system.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">Osmani distinguishes exploratory prompting from production practices with design documents, test-driven changes, review and ownership. He argues that treating either workflow as universally appropriate obscures the requirements of maintenance-intensive software.</data>
  <data key="d264">Fast conversational prototyping and accountable AI-assisted engineering are distinct development regimes.</data>
  <data key="d265">Choose rigor appropriate to the target environment; Require explicit acceptance contracts for production work; Teach the transition from prototype to maintainable system.</data>
