  <data key="d226">https://addyo.substack.com/p/the-reality-of-ai-assisted-software</data>
  <data key="d173">2025-08-16</data>
  <data key="d79">Perceived personal acceleration with coding AI does not necessarily translate into net team or release-level productivity.</data>
  <data key="d80">The percentages reported by Osmani come from diverse third-party surveys and experiments; no single pooled causal estimate is supplied.</data>
  <data key="d81">Use task-adjusted and quality-adjusted metrics; Report study context before citing a percentage; Separate survey sentiment, experiments and shipped-value outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d82">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d86">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d85">Practitioner essay / technical guidance (not peer-reviewed)</data>
  <data key="d83">A</data>
  <data key="d87">article webpage read; linked empirical sources not all independently audited</data>
  <data key="d93">The article synthesizes surveys and selected field studies showing variation by task, developer and codebase. It cautions against treating high adoption, code generation or self-reported speed as direct evidence of deployment throughput or organizational value.</data>
  <data key="d264">Perceived personal acceleration with coding AI does not necessarily translate into net team or release-level productivity.</data>
  <data key="d265">Use task-adjusted and quality-adjusted metrics; Report study context before citing a percentage; Separate survey sentiment, experiments and shipped-value outcomes.</data>
