  <data key="d300">newsletter</data>
  <data key="d301">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d302"></data>
  <data key="d303">[]</data>
  <data key="d79">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d264">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d93">Alexey Komissarouk describes experimentation-driven engineering that prioritizes learning about business outcomes, supported by product analytics, feature flags and organizational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d265">Offers a useful contrast between shipping to learn and building for longevity. Reported business experiments are not evaluations of AI-assisted development.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Revenue and experimental effects are contributor-reported and not independently replicated here. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Growth engineering connects product hypotheses to measured outcomes rather than treating feature output as value.</data>
