  <data key="d79">Discusses employer experiences with automated applications and AI-assisted interview deception, alongside possible changes to remote hiring, trial periods and work samples.</data>
  <data key="d264">Discusses employer experiences with automated applications and AI-assisted interview deception, alongside possible changes to remote hiring, trial periods and work samples.</data>
  <data key="d93">Discusses employer experiences with automated applications and AI-assisted interview deception, alongside possible changes to remote hiring, trial periods and work samples.</data>
  <data key="d265">The visible cases suggest that hiring signals require reassessment; they do not demonstrate that remote interviews universally fail or in-person hiring is inevitable.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Orosz discloses an investment in Maestro, one of the companies discussed. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Employer experiences with AI-assisted applications and interviews inform hiring policy; the blog is only a partial alternate edition and no software-delivery effect is estimated.</data>
