  <data key="d264">Chip Huyen’s book excerpt distinguishes application, model and infrastructure layers and compares AI engineering with machine-learning and full-stack engineering.</data>
  <data key="d93">Chip Huyen’s book excerpt distinguishes application, model and infrastructure layers and compares AI engineering with machine-learning and full-stack engineering. Evaluation and interfaces are central application concerns.</data>
  <data key="d265">Provides an architectural vocabulary for building AI products; it should not be treated as evidence that using AI improves software-development productivity.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Excerpt credited to Chip Huyen; primarily software engineering for AI, not AI-assisted software engineering. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
