  <data key="d93">Uses an interview with Downdetector engineering leadership to examine why a multi-cloud monitoring service still depended on Cloudflare.</data>
  <data key="d265">Reliability depends on the complete dependency chain; removing a dependency can carry substantial cost and operational burden. This is a contextual trade-off, not proof that redundancy is unnecessary.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Non-Pulse-titled public excerpt of Pulse #154. This non-Pulse-titled blog article is an excerpt of a Pulse issue originally published 2025-11-20. It passes the literal title-prefix rule; it is excluded by the optional stricter Pulse-origin filter. The parent issue is provenance only, not another P article. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">An availability architecture trades dependency risk against operational cost; it is not an AI-specific ROI study.</data>
