  <data key="d79">Reports rebuilding a small testimonials feature with Codex, including planning, modular data, testing and deployment.</data>
  <data key="d264">Reports rebuilding a small testimonials feature with Codex, including planning, modular data, testing and deployment.</data>
  <data key="d93">Reports rebuilding a small testimonials feature with Codex, including planning, modular data, testing and deployment. The replacement covered a narrower personal use case than the original service.</data>
  <data key="d265">Demonstrates a bounded build-versus-buy example, not the general replacement of SaaS. Maintenance, verification and changing compliance obligations remain outside the headline time comparison.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">The reported replacement covers the personal functionality the author used, not the complete SaaS product; lifecycle maintenance and opportunity costs were not measured. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">The personal build-versus-buy experiment has a narrow scope; the headline omits long-term maintenance and service equivalence.</data>
