  <data key="d93">A written interview explores Yegge’s autonomy ladder, multi-agent work, fatigue and predictions about engineering employment.</data>
  <data key="d265">These are provocative practitioner forecasts, not validated maturity levels or labor-market estimates. Higher autonomy is not established as inherently better.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Yegge’s eight stages are a provocative practitioner ladder, not a validated maturity scale and not Osmani’s independent agency/orchestration axes. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Yegge's levels and forecasts describe a practitioner's model of agent work, not a validated maturity scale.</data>
