  <data key="d93">Orosz contrasts increased generation and pull-request activity with quality problems, cleanup, outages and organizational mandates.</data>
  <data key="d265">Activity can rise without corresponding product value. Claims drawn from underlying studies require separate source verification before causal use.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Observed product bugs and the author’s inference that AI caused them are different claims. Visible anecdotes do not identify a causal quality effect. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">The synthesis highlights downstream cleanup and review load rather than equating more generated changes with more value.</data>
