  <data key="d79">Revisits forward-deployed engineering through two disappointed practitioners and external hiring coverage, contrasting role marketing with sales and customer-delivery duties.</data>
  <data key="d264">Revisits forward-deployed engineering through two disappointed practitioners and external hiring coverage, contrasting role marketing with sales and customer-delivery duties.</data>
  <data key="d93">Revisits forward-deployed engineering through two disappointed practitioners and external hiring coverage, contrasting role marketing with sales and customer-delivery duties.</data>
  <data key="d265">The examples qualify an earlier positive account: identical job titles can hide substantially different engineering responsibilities. They do not establish market-wide dissatisfaction rates.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Non-Pulse-titled blog excerpt; not a duplicate of the longer August 2025 Deepdive. This non-Pulse-titled blog article is an excerpt of a Pulse issue originally published 2026-03-19. It passes the literal title-prefix rule; it is excluded by the optional stricter Pulse-origin filter. The parent issue is provenance only, not another P article. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">A small set of dissatisfied accounts qualifies FDE enthusiasm; it does not estimate role-wide job satisfaction.</data>
