  <data key="d78">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/tech-jobs-market-in-2026-part-3-hiring</data>
  <data key="d168">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/tech-jobs-market-in-2026-part-3-hiring</data>
  <data key="d226">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/tech-jobs-market-in-2026-part-3-hiring</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-07-07</data>
  <data key="d294">Canonical article edition date; earlier identified parent-issue date retained separately</data>
  <data key="d295">2026-07-07</data>
  <data key="d296">2026-07-07</data>
  <data key="d297">NO_PULSE_ORIGIN_IDENTIFIED</data>
  <data key="d298"></data>
  <data key="d299">true</data>
  <data key="d300">newsletter</data>
  <data key="d301">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d302"></data>
  <data key="d303">[]</data>
  <data key="d79">Accounts from hiring managers and job seekers describe noisy applications, distrust of AI-enhanced credentials and sharply different demand across specialties and regions.</data>
  <data key="d264">Accounts from hiring managers and job seekers describe noisy applications, distrust of AI-enhanced credentials and sharply different demand across specialties and regions.</data>
  <data key="d93">Accounts from hiring managers and job seekers describe noisy applications, distrust of AI-enhanced credentials and sharply different demand across specialties and regions. This complements, rather than duplicates, the series’ vacancy-data analyses.</data>
  <data key="d265">Reported hiring friction can coexist with hard-to-fill positions. Interview accounts cannot estimate the industry-wide employment effect of AI or eliminate selection bias.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
