  <data key="d79">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption.</data>
  <data key="d264">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption.</data>
  <data key="d93">A company deepdive introduces trading-specific engineering incentives, tightly integrated hardware/software, platform ownership, risk management and AI adoption. The public introduction contrasts low-latency execution with increasingly important predictive models.</data>
  <data key="d265">Speed is constrained by the consequences of failure. Trading-specific architecture and incentives are useful boundary conditions, not a template for every development team.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80"> Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Trading-system constraints provide an important boundary case for engineering controls; do not generalize domain-specific incentives.</data>
