<node id="P114">
  <data key="d73">Headed for the Exit: the Great Engineering Leader Career Break</data>
  <data key="d74">practitioner_article</data>
  <data key="d96">CURATED_PRACTITIONER_NOT_PEER_REVIEWED_RESEARCH</data>
  <data key="d75">Jobs &amp; roles</data>
  <data key="d76">2026</data>
  <data key="d293">Gergely Orosz</data>
  <data key="d78">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/the-great-engineering-leader-career-break</data>
  <data key="d168">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/the-great-engineering-leader-career-break</data>
  <data key="d226">https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/the-great-engineering-leader-career-break</data>
  <data key="d173">2026-08-18</data>
  <data key="d294">Canonical article edition date; earlier identified parent-issue date retained separately</data>
  <data key="d295">2026-08-18</data>
  <data key="d296">2026-08-18</data>
  <data key="d297">NO_PULSE_ORIGIN_IDENTIFIED</data>
  <data key="d298"></data>
  <data key="d299">true</data>
  <data key="d300">newsletter</data>
  <data key="d301">Deepdives</data>
  <data key="d302"></data>
  <data key="d303">[]</data>
  <data key="d79">Interviews with engineering leaders examine career breaks, founder expectations, cost pressure, changing team sizes and renewed interest in hands-on work.</data>
  <data key="d264">Interviews with engineering leaders examine career breaks, founder expectations, cost pressure, changing team sizes and renewed interest in hands-on work.</data>
  <data key="d93">Interviews with engineering leaders examine career breaks, founder expectations, cost pressure, changing team sizes and renewed interest in hands-on work. The preview highlights tension between rapid prototyping and operational ownership.</data>
  <data key="d265">The interviews identify plausible mechanisms and experiences, not the prevalence of leadership departures or a causal effect of AI on employment.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Selected career-break interviews and the six-of-ten subgroup do not estimate a population departure rate. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Leadership-break interviews concern ownership, incentives and transitions, without measuring the prevalence of AI-caused exits.</data>
  <data key="d82">Industry/practitioner publication — qualitative industry interviews</data>
  <data key="d86">Industry/practitioner publication — qualitative industry interviews</data>
