  <data key="d93">The article surveys responses to growing AI-generated review workloads: reviewing AI feedback, routing by blast radius, inspecting plans and tests, reducing patch size, and retaining manual review.</data>
  <data key="d265">The visible discussion rejects a universal review process. Noise filtering, scope decisions and release responsibility remain important even when review automation increases.</data>
