  <data key="d79">A company-visit report describes Codex adoption, internal integrations and feedback loops extending into performance work and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d264">A company-visit report describes Codex adoption, internal integrations and feedback loops extending into performance work and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d93">A company-visit report describes Codex adoption, internal integrations and feedback loops extending into performance work and infrastructure. Its public preview emphasizes harness capabilities and changes in engineering responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d265">An unusually integrated environment and effectively unrestricted internal token access limit generalization. Claimed adoption and productivity implications require separate outcome measurement.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Internal integrations, selected interviewees and unusually permissive token budgets limit transfer to other organizations. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">A deeply integrated internal software factory is a boundary case, not a representative operating environment.</data>
