  <data key="d79">The public preview examines Shopify’s return to native mobile development after previously adopting React Native.</data>
  <data key="d264">The public preview examines Shopify’s return to native mobile development after previously adopting React Native.</data>
  <data key="d93">The public preview examines Shopify’s return to native mobile development after previously adopting React Native. It connects AI-assisted implementation with changing performance and code-sharing trade-offs.</data>
  <data key="d265">Reported migration speed is company-specific; the preview also recognizes that AI can assist native and cross-platform stacks. It does not prove that native development is universally superior.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">A selected team’s reported migration does not establish that React Native or cross-platform development is generally obsolete. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">AI can change platform migration costs, but a single-company account does not establish universal superiority of native development.</data>
