  <data key="d79">Orosz synthesizes company visits, interviews and platform data in a keynote about agent-heavy development.</data>
  <data key="d264">Orosz synthesizes company visits, interviews and platform data in a keynote about agent-heavy development.</data>
  <data key="d93">Orosz synthesizes company visits, interviews and platform data in a keynote about agent-heavy development. He contrasts changing interfaces and review workloads with the continuing importance of teams, planning and verification.</data>
  <data key="d265">Reported frontier practices are a directional snapshot, not representative adoption estimates. Increased code volume does not establish increased delivered value.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">The article contains an apparent October 2025/2026 date inconsistency in its PR-volume discussion; do not import those numerical estimates without primary-source checking. The October 2025 phrase still conflicts with the October 2026 publication and August 2026 PR discussion. Keep the author’s numerical extrapolation unresolved rather than silently changing its date. The article explicitly synthesizes earlier P-series reporting. Public availability does not imply an independent check of every paragraph or chart. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">A keynote synthesis summarizes frontier practices and preserves engineering fundamentals; overlapping reporting is not fresh experimental evidence.</data>
