  <data key="d79">Orosz edits a Beck–Fowler panel discussion about AI and earlier technological shifts.</data>
  <data key="d264">Orosz edits a Beck–Fowler panel discussion about AI and earlier technological shifts.</data>
  <data key="d93">Orosz edits a Beck–Fowler panel discussion about AI and earlier technological shifts. The public outline connects adoption, team practice, workload, outcome metrics, testing and craft.</data>
  <data key="d265">The visible discussion argues for curiosity tempered by skepticism. The outline proposes attention to outcomes, work boundaries and engineering practice; these are participant recommendations, not measured productivity or retention effects.</data>
  <data key="d304">Visible arguments, author-reported observations and explicitly labeled outlines; no reconstruction of hidden sections.</data>
  <data key="d80">Only the public introduction, outline and opening discussion were inspected; the paid remainder was not accessed. Beck and Fowler are participants, not article byline coauthors. The Summit also informs P088, so these articles are not independent event evidence. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d81">Directly addresses using AI in software work, with historical and organizational analogies; maps to shipped value and agile team practices as editorial proposals.</data>
