<node id="B006">
  <data key="d73">The Experience Divide</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter03_v3.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">2c277baece8dabb6c495ca69c1c29803ec769bf2f0a9e0054bf3f73794a839b8</data>
  <data key="d365">392</data>
  <data key="d366">3477</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B006.md</data>
  <data key="d264">L’esperienza cambia il modo in cui si delega all’AI, ma va preservato il ciclo di apprendimento.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo analizza falsa sicurezza, trio programming e trasformazione delle competenze per junior, intermedi e senior. Offre un ponte fra produttività individuale e formazione del team.</data>
  <data key="d80">Le classi di esperienza non sono gruppi sperimentali; le prescrizioni formative richiedono misure di comprensione, retention e trasferimento.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Skills &amp; learning</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Jobs &amp; roles"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Skills formation and teaching", "K:Cognitive offloading and skill debt", "K:Employment and early-career roles", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C10", "C:C12"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Why Experience Matters More Than Ever", "line": 27, "offset": 2901, "end": 2948}, {"level": "section", "title": "Preserving the Learning Loop", "line": 95, "offset": 8406, "end": 8444}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Skill Transformation", "line": 221, "offset": 18000, "end": 18034}, {"level": "section", "title": "Control, Confidence, and Understanding", "line": 356, "offset": 25951, "end": 25999}]</data>
