<node id="B007">
  <data key="d73">New Workflows for the AI Era</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter04_v5.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">763822b37c388a0fe474f8e30be03eb08bc48ecdae910167bb8116e5c2b6b2f3</data>
  <data key="d365">987</data>
  <data key="d366">7757</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B007.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Workflow piccoli e verificabili trasformano l’AI da generatore a componente del processo ingegneristico.</data>
  <data key="d93">Pianificazione, TDD, runtime feedback, contesto, review e orchestrazione enterprise sono raccolti in un percorso operativo. Il file è il principale punto di origine di varie elaborazioni dei volumi successivi.</data>
  <data key="d80">Le descrizioni dei workflow non misurano automaticamente un vantaggio di velocità o qualità; mantenere le dipendenze fra i controlli.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Human-agent collaboration", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:Long-running agent execution"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C04", "C:C07", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Workflow: Plan Before You Prompt", "line": 17, "offset": 1293, "end": 1335}, {"level": "section", "title": "Workflow: Keeping the Runtime in the Loop", "line": 215, "offset": 17257, "end": 17308}, {"level": "section", "title": "Workflow: Understanding Legacy Systems", "line": 549, "offset": 42402, "end": 42450}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Orchestration Mindset", "line": 920, "offset": 68678, "end": 68713}]</data>
