<node id="B014">
  <data key="d73">PART II: Quality Assurance</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter07/chapter07_part2.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">ddaab92e52b76bea22a86d4c6fad3960863640c1ad8eca08d599e9aeb4ff6843</data>
  <data key="d365">1077</data>
  <data key="d366">3505</data>
  <data key="d367">section</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B014.md</data>
  <data key="d264">I pattern di assurance collegano sicurezza, revisione graduata e comprensione del legacy.</data>
  <data key="d93">Security-first, review gauntlet e legacy navigation organizzano controlli e responsabilità prima dell’approvazione dei cambiamenti.</data>
  <data key="d80">Una checklist o una review multi-pass non costituisce da sola un controllo indipendente; contano input, oracoli e copertura.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Code quality &amp; security</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Skills &amp; learning"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Prompt injection and malicious tools", "K:Vulnerability and secure code", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:AI as reviewer", "K:Automation bias and trust", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Onboarding and developer fluency", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C05", "C:C06", "C:C08", "C:C09"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "PART II: Quality Assurance", "line": 3, "offset": 2, "end": 39}]</data>
