<node id="B016">
  <data key="d73">PART IV: Organizational Foundation</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter07/chapter07_part4.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">9d668054284384874a1722dd095b05a02c83d3e3b643c76dc189fa31da25ff1a</data>
  <data key="d365">1203</data>
  <data key="d366">3570</data>
  <data key="d367">section</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B016.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Le fondamenta organizzative rendono espliciti abilitazione, policy, misura e costi.</data>
  <data key="d93">I pattern 15–18 coprono programma di formazione, acceptable use policy, ciclo di misura-apprendimento e gestione della spesa.</data>
  <data key="d80">Esempi aziendali e framework economici non sono repliche indipendenti né garanzie di ROI trasferibile.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:Productivity", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Economics"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer", "K:Economic costs and return", "K:Output versus shipped value"]</data>
