<node id="B018">
  <data key="d73">Antipatterns: What Not to Do</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter07/chapter07_antipatterns.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">8cc39f88bf8b3b98d17205a97205e44cc26da2a0ecb460ef0d488908c10043a4</data>
  <data key="d365">298</data>
  <data key="d366">1278</data>
  <data key="d367">section</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B018.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Gli antipattern mostrano come velocità apparente e delega cieca erodano affidabilità e apprendimento.</data>
  <data key="d93">Accettazione acritica, trappola del 70%, produzione senza verifica, contesto assente, batch eccessivi e misura teatrale formano una griglia diagnostica.</data>
  <data key="d80">Il catalogo identifica rischi plausibili; non stima frequenza, severità o effetto causale degli antipattern.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Productivity"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:AI as reviewer", "K:Automation bias and trust", "K:Cognitive offloading and skill debt", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer", "K:Controlled productivity evidence", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C02", "C:C08", "C:C10"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Antipatterns: What Not to Do", "line": 5, "offset": 4, "end": 43}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
