<node id="B020">
  <data key="d73">Understanding Tool Maturity Levels</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter10/01_maturity_levels.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">03dbba47d7945250e812fd53c8e722015d520811b40ff0fd83c79aa2d63d3b21</data>
  <data key="d365">151</data>
  <data key="d366">646</data>
  <data key="d367">section</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B020.md</data>
  <data key="d264">I livelli di maturità aiutano a distinguere esplorazione, prova e adozione.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il file propone di interpretare classificazioni tipo Technology Radar e di far evolvere la scelta attraverso esperienza locale e revisione periodica.</data>
  <data key="d80">Le etichette ASSESS/TRIAL/ADOPT sono raccomandazioni contestuali e datate, non punteggi di affidabilità universali.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:Productivity", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Controlled productivity evidence"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C02", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Understanding Tool Maturity Levels", "line": 3, "offset": 2, "end": 46}]</data>
