<node id="B025">
  <data key="d73">From Single Agent to Multi-Agent Workflows</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V01</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter10/06_multi_agent.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">0cdb4fb9d02a3fdf228a76b853e4d4c51db6999b0eb13acc4ad75626ad216bbd</data>
  <data key="d365">487</data>
  <data key="d366">2714</data>
  <data key="d367">section</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V01/B025.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il passaggio a più agenti richiede specializzazione, confini e punti di controllo.</data>
  <data key="d93">La sezione distingue subagent e workflow multi-agente, associando integrazione enterprise, condivisione del contesto e checkpoint umani.</data>
  <data key="d80">Il parallelismo non dimostra maggiore produttività; occorre contabilizzare errori di coordinamento e revisione seriale.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Human-agent collaboration", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "From Single Agent to Multi-Agent Workflows", "line": 2, "offset": 1, "end": 53}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
