<node id="B038">
  <data key="d73">The Shift</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V02</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG/chapters/chapter01_shift.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">1a91b066014e9e6b3a16028d28873509535d11dc4643cdb4f4976d63d37187df</data>
  <data key="d365">421</data>
  <data key="d366">3280</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V02/B038.md</data>
  <data key="d264">L’intento diventa la fonte di riferimento del processo, con confini di autorità espliciti.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo oppone code-first e intent-first, formula cinque principi e introduce il sistema di confini a tre livelli.</data>
  <data key="d80">I principi sono prescrizioni progettuali, non una dimostrazione che ogni specifica sia completa o corretta.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Specifications and governance", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C04", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "From Code-First to Intent-First", "line": 15, "offset": 529, "end": 570}, {"level": "section", "title": "Vibe Coding vs.\\ Spec-Driven Development", "line": 85, "offset": 5684, "end": 5734}, {"level": "section", "title": "Five Principles That Actually Work", "line": 142, "offset": 10759, "end": 10803}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Three-Tier Boundary System", "line": 260, "offset": 19455, "end": 19495}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
