<node id="B051">
  <data key="d73">Anatomy of an AI SDD Framework</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter03_anatomy.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">3c9e70a2ae890e4300cbed66e1c7e86559ecd40c0815ac9937d1e618b4320059</data>
  <data key="d365">426</data>
  <data key="d366">5133</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B051.md</data>
  <data key="d264">I framework vengono scomposti in istruzioni, prompt, agenti e skill su diversi substrati.</data>
  <data key="d93">La tassonomia delle primitive e le regole di composizione permettono di confrontare implementazioni apparentemente diverse e di leggere le strutture dei repository.</data>
  <data key="d80">La tassonomia è una sintesi progettuale dell’autore; la somiglianza delle strutture non implica identità di comportamento o qualità.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:System knowledge &amp; memory</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Dependencies and agent supply chain", "K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Specifications and governance"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C04", "C:C09"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Why Frameworks Look Alike Underneath", "line": 15, "offset": 919, "end": 965}, {"level": "section", "title": "Primitive 3 --- Agents", "line": 152, "offset": 11392, "end": 11424}, {"level": "section", "title": "Where the Primitives Live in the Three Big Harnesses", "line": 285, "offset": 22622, "end": 22684}, {"level": "section", "title": "What to Look For When You Read Part II", "line": 396, "offset": 33860, "end": 33908}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
