<node id="B053">
  <data key="d73">The Lightweight Protocols: GSD v1 and GSD-2</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter05_gsd.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">9f1b1ebed1f3956520fc13d642ded6df5bc2479d436ca3a40b33e65cf724e1df</data>
  <data key="d365">303</data>
  <data key="d366">3954</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B053.md</data>
  <data key="d264">GSD v1 e GSD-2 rappresentano due modi di ottenere disciplina con poco processo.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il confronto combina workflow leggeri, evoluzione strutturata e una simulazione di autenticazione JWT per rendere visibili artefatti e transizioni.</data>
  <data key="d80">La field-test simulation resta una simulazione didattica, non un confronto controllato eseguito sui prodotti attuali.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:What agents can do"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Specifications and governance", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Long-running agent execution"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C04"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Lightweight Philosophy", "line": 16, "offset": 403, "end": 439}, {"level": "section", "title": "GSD v1 --- Action-Oriented Protocol", "line": 33, "offset": 2928, "end": 2973}, {"level": "section", "title": "Field-Test Simulation: JWT Authentication", "line": 203, "offset": 23010, "end": 23061}, {"level": "section", "title": "Lessons for Your Practice", "line": 241, "offset": 25845, "end": 25880}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
