<node id="B054">
  <data key="d73">The Specification Toolkits: Spec Kit and OpenSpec (openspec.dev)</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter06_spectools.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">a803100f32d0ed9bb03506561afe3e44e8e838131df018e142c312206c9c9ea2</data>
  <data key="d365">814</data>
  <data key="d366">10419</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B054.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Spec Kit e OpenSpec affrontano specificazione e cambiamento brownfield con strutture diverse.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo compara toolchain, delta specification, chiarimento prima del piano e una simulazione JWT, esplicitando trade-off e scelte di design.</data>
  <data key="d80">Comandi e lifecycle vanno letti nella versione fornita; il confronto non dimostra la superiorità generale di uno strumento.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Specifications and governance", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Independent verification and oracles"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C04", "C:C05"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Spec Kit --- The Specification Toolchain", "line": 23, "offset": 1281, "end": 1331}, {"level": "section", "title": "Spec Kit vs.\\ OpenSpec: A Direct Comparison", "line": 496, "offset": 54876, "end": 54929}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Clarify-Before-Plan Pattern", "line": 585, "offset": 63086, "end": 63127}, {"level": "section", "title": "Lessons for Your Practice", "line": 766, "offset": 77336, "end": 77371}]</data>
