<node id="B056">
  <data key="d73">Autonomous Loops and Behavioral Foundations</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter08_autonomous.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">5bff2e88df8bb7940b34d377d69d9b488bb0ba5100b4278946676015b0e011df</data>
  <data key="d365">629</data>
  <data key="d366">10585</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B056.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Loop autonomi e disciplina comportamentale sono componenti da comporre, non alternative equivalenti.</data>
  <data key="d93">Ralph Copilot, Spec Loop Engine, skill ispirate a Karpathy, Agent Skills e AIDD sono letti attraverso autonomia, vincoli e una simulazione di implementazione.</data>
  <data key="d80">I profili e la simulazione non costituiscono un benchmark; distinguere regole suggerite e controlli realmente applicati dal runtime.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Engineering structure"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Specifications and governance"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C04", "C:C07"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Autonomy Spectrum", "line": 20, "offset": 1167, "end": 1198}, {"level": "section", "title": "Karpathy-Inspired Skills --- Behavioral Discipline", "line": 257, "offset": 34923, "end": 34983}, {"level": "section", "title": "AIDD --- Architecture-Decision-Driven Backend Pipeline", "line": 426, "offset": 52965, "end": 53029}, {"level": "section", "title": "Lessons for Your Practice", "line": 581, "offset": 73480, "end": 73515}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
