<node id="B058">
  <data key="d73">Design Boundaries: What to Adopt, What to Avoid</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter10_boundaries.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">f4e89dfab7a1b75f618433de0d8423b30f82d62a3d6994071abcf7352c46d135</data>
  <data key="d365">403</data>
  <data key="d366">5427</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B058.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il framework adatto è quello con rigore sufficiente e costo proporzionato.</data>
  <data key="d93">Tre livelli di rigore, griglia di adozione, antipattern, migrazione e complementarità definiscono confini per evitare accumulo indiscriminato di meccanismi.</data>
  <data key="d80">La selezione va verificata su rischi e vincoli locali; la tassonomia non rende equivalenti strumenti complementari.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:Productivity", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C04", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Three Tiers of Rigor", "line": 20, "offset": 756, "end": 790}, {"level": "section", "title": "Eight Anti-Patterns from the Wild", "line": 198, "offset": 19317, "end": 19360}, {"level": "section", "title": "What an Ideal Framework Would Combine", "line": 304, "offset": 29330, "end": 29377}, {"level": "section", "title": "Design Boundaries of Enterprise SDD", "line": 363, "offset": 36495, "end": 36540}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
