<node id="B062">
  <data key="d73">Autonomous Execution: Modes, Budgets, and Governance</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter14_autonomy.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">484cf12509a4ef84dc7b2cb0174d8248a02443f033596e8667c04a8c7ea944dc</data>
  <data key="d365">748</data>
  <data key="d366">7795</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B062.md</data>
  <data key="d264">L’autonomia viene trattata come policy di esecuzione con budget ed escalation.</data>
  <data key="d93">Tre modalità, un elemento per ciclo, evidence pack, convergence review e casi enterprise definiscono cosa l’agente può fare e quando deve fermarsi.</data>
  <data key="d80">Budget e audit-after non sostituiscono criteri di accettazione indipendenti; gli esempi non provano sicurezza in produzione.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Economics", "T:Productivity"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer", "K:Economic costs and return", "K:Output versus shipped value"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C11", "C:C12"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Use Case 1: The Friday Afternoon Decision", "line": 28, "offset": 1445, "end": 1496}, {"level": "section", "title": "The One-Item-Per-Cycle Protocol", "line": 231, "offset": 16911, "end": 16952}, {"level": "section", "title": "Convergence Review", "line": 528, "offset": 37242, "end": 37270}, {"level": "section", "title": "Use Case 2: Greenfield Enterprise Java with Kafka", "line": 684, "offset": 49241, "end": 49300}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
