<node id="B064">
  <data key="d73">Limitations and Professional Judgment</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter16_limitations.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">c726789bc12ceb26cbed18d715409013fc83a4e244e8e90615cb413e05ee2ea6</data>
  <data key="d365">542</data>
  <data key="d366">7471</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B064.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il giudizio professionale stabilisce quando ridurre, modificare o non usare SDD.</data>
  <data key="d93">Rapporti di campo, anti-casi, overhead, gate skipping, spec rot e attriti organizzativi delimitano la portata del metodo.</data>
  <data key="d80">Witboost e Mollie sono resoconti del corpus, non pilot replicati qui; confronto e generalizzazione richiedono protocolli e denominatori.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Productivity", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:What agents can do"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Specifications and governance", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Controlled productivity evidence", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Agent failure and escalation"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C02", "C:C04", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Two Field Reports: Witboost and Mollie", "line": 20, "offset": 705, "end": 753}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Overhead Tax", "line": 184, "offset": 16802, "end": 16828}, {"level": "section", "title": "The AI Reliability Gap", "line": 335, "offset": 31115, "end": 31147}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Professional Developer's Heuristic", "line": 454, "offset": 44673, "end": 44721}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
