<node id="B079">
  <data key="d73">Karpathy-Inspired Skills</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Spec-driven Development — 2nd edition</data>
  <data key="d364">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/appendices/reference_cards/appendix_karpathy.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">3c84a699d6381f3230a19d991e5b763b7f0a681bad6c2b161040ea230f8dcd3c</data>
  <data key="d365">81</data>
  <data key="d366">599</data>
  <data key="d367">reference_card</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V03/B079.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Le skill ispirate a Karpathy sono principi comportamentali, non una pipeline SDLC.</data>
  <data key="d93">La scheda separa disciplina di lavoro, comportamento dell’agente e assenza di comandi o artefatti di processo propri.</data>
  <data key="d80">Non confrontare questo insieme di principi con una toolchain come se avesse la stessa unità funzionale o le stesse garanzie.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:What agents can do", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Skills formation and teaching", "K:Cognitive offloading and skill debt"]</data>
