<node id="B086">
  <data key="d73">The Philosophy of Deterministic Failure</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter02_philosophy.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">e5877964bca2d35f772986e072b4087b75792a15e89705c2015c204ac06d6dfe</data>
  <data key="d365">490</data>
  <data key="d366">5021</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B086.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Progettare per il fallimento prevedibile significa fornire segnali di rifiuto e stato recuperabile.</data>
  <data key="d93">Backpressure, test, contesto fresco, piano modificabile e memoria su disco spostano l’attenzione dal prompt perfetto alle condizioni che bloccano lavoro invalido.</data>
  <data key="d80">Il controllo respinge soltanto ciò che sa riconoscere; LLM-as-judge e soglia contestuale 40–60% richiedono qualificazione e verifica nel contesto d’uso.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C07", "C:C09"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Embracing Predictable Failure", "line": 18, "offset": 1425, "end": 1464}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Backpressure Model", "line": 96, "offset": 7874, "end": 7906}, {"level": "section", "title": "Core Principles for Autonomous Systems", "line": 289, "offset": 24588, "end": 24636}, {"level": "section", "title": "Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid", "line": 444, "offset": 34444, "end": 34483}]</data>
