<node id="B087">
  <data key="d73">The Developer Evolution Model</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter03_evolution.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">8100340c3982a08db0283347394523f0ebfca3a026102da8fce8992f9d085db4</data>
  <data key="d365">395</data>
  <data key="d366">4034</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B087.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il modello a nove stadi rende discutibili competenze e prerequisiti della delega agli agenti.</data>
  <data key="d93">La progressione è usata per autovalutare pratiche di sviluppo, trasformazione delle abilità e preparazione a sistemi autonomi.</data>
  <data key="d80">È una tassonomia didattica, non una scala validata. Il confronto con gli otto stadi attribuiti a Yegge nel corpus P richiede distinguere adattamento e citazione letterale.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Skills &amp; learning", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Jobs &amp; roles"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Skills formation and teaching", "K:Cognitive offloading and skill debt", "K:Employment and early-career roles", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C10", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Nine Stages of AI-Assisted Development", "line": 17, "offset": 1584, "end": 1636}, {"level": "section", "title": "Assessing Your Current Stage", "line": 182, "offset": 15152, "end": 15190}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Skills Transformation", "line": 264, "offset": 21273, "end": 21308}, {"level": "section", "title": "Prerequisites for This Book", "line": 321, "offset": 25248, "end": 25285}]</data>
