<node id="B089">
  <data key="d73">Task Decomposition for Machines</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter05_decomposition.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">4891c821bb6f814c065b12abb79194075ef3e9d7536433cbeff318c1dbf87b7f</data>
  <data key="d365">703</data>
  <data key="d366">4538</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B089.md</data>
  <data key="d264">La decomposizione rende una richiesta eseguibile attraverso unità limitate e criteri verificabili.</data>
  <data key="d93">Dal PRD al piano strutturato, il capitolo descrive caratteristiche dei task, schema del file e criteri di accettazione con un esempio completo.</data>
  <data key="d80">La piccola dimensione dei task non risolve dipendenze e ambiguità; la specifica deve restare indipendente dall’implementazione candidata.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Code quality &amp; security"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Specifications and governance", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C04", "C:C07"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "From PRD to Executable Tasks", "line": 24, "offset": 2132, "end": 2170}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Plan File Schema", "line": 225, "offset": 16456, "end": 16486}, {"level": "section", "title": "Writing Effective Acceptance Criteria", "line": 352, "offset": 21732, "end": 21779}, {"level": "section", "title": "A Complete Worked Example", "line": 506, "offset": 29459, "end": 29494}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
