<node id="B091">
  <data key="d73">Quality Gates and Backpressure</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter07_quality.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">9eff56f237ad4042054343dcb9d2fb82b5b74ac0a6c30d2b80e683c84abb7445</data>
  <data key="d365">661</data>
  <data key="d366">4311</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B091.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Quality gate e backpressure trasformano gli errori in rifiuti operativi anziché in accettazioni apparenti.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo compone test, verifica, gestione degli stalli e giudici linguistici, con configurazioni ed esempio applicativo.</data>
  <data key="d80">La separazione dei ruoli e l’auto-critica non garantiscono indipendenza; un caso illustrativo non misura la probabilità residua di difetto.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:What agents can do"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:AI as reviewer", "K:Automation bias and trust", "K:Agent failure and escalation"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C07", "C:C08"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Quality Checks in the Loop", "line": 18, "offset": 1498, "end": 1534}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Verification Loop Pattern", "line": 241, "offset": 15011, "end": 15050}, {"level": "section", "title": "LLM-as-Judge for Subjective Criteria", "line": 399, "offset": 24035, "end": 24081}, {"level": "section", "title": "Case Study: Quality Gates in Action", "line": 599, "offset": 32676, "end": 32721}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
