<node id="B093">
  <data key="d73">Agentic Patterns in Practice</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter09_patterns.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">3c88f9e5d7b0288e46de69503668ac80ecb7778165d80bf74eab10da30c4e2ba</data>
  <data key="d365">558</data>
  <data key="d366">4607</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B093.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il catalogo organizza pattern agentici per controllo, memoria, feedback, affidabilità e sicurezza.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo propone composizione e selezione dei pattern, esplicitando anche collaborazione, ambiente e aggiornamento del repertorio.</data>
  <data key="d80">Una tassonomia ampia non dimostra il beneficio di aggiungere componenti; coordinamento e costi devono giustificare ogni meccanismo.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Engineering structure</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Engineering structure", "T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Developer workflow and adoption", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Human-agent collaboration", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Prompt injection and malicious tools", "K:Vulnerability and secure code"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C06", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Pattern Landscape", "line": 20, "offset": 1954, "end": 1985}, {"level": "section", "title": "Learning \\&amp; Adaptation Patterns", "line": 252, "offset": 17570, "end": 17611}, {"level": "section", "title": "Tool Use \\&amp; Environment Patterns", "line": 327, "offset": 23849, "end": 23891}, {"level": "section", "title": "Staying Current", "line": 516, "offset": 34498, "end": 34523}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
