<node id="B094">
  <data key="d73">Scheduling and Overnight Execution</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter09b_scheduling.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">ea1858d0de0f786aa947e1c33e48c1aaa43998e755ec2e84526a795cc92e9f76</data>
  <data key="d365">933</data>
  <data key="d366">3890</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B094.md</data>
  <data key="d264">L’esecuzione notturna richiede una sequenza controllata di job, non soltanto un timer.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il file distingue revisione cumulativa e lavoro autonomo, descrive schedulatori per sistemi operativi diversi, esecuzione cloud e notifiche.</data>
  <data key="d80">L’ordine temporale deve essere verificato come dipendenza e recupero dagli errori; l’avvio schedulato non autorizza merge o deployment.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C09", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Two-Job Sequence", "line": 24, "offset": 1985, "end": 2015}, {"level": "section", "title": "Scheduling on Linux (systemd/cron)", "line": 381, "offset": 15906, "end": 15950}, {"level": "section", "title": "Scheduling on Windows", "line": 501, "offset": 19422, "end": 19453}, {"level": "section", "title": "Monitoring and Notification", "line": 733, "offset": 28592, "end": 28629}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
