<node id="B095">
  <data key="d73">Multi-Agent Orchestration</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V04</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Autonomous Coding Agents</data>
  <data key="d364">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter10_orchestration.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">8f3c5c3e2f05c774aba371e5d85f132b2483dfde5357552d72c4ee3f7d95fe1c</data>
  <data key="d365">744</data>
  <data key="d366">4996</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V04/B095.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il multi-agente diventa utile quando isolamento e coordinamento risolvono un limite osservato del singolo loop.</data>
  <data key="d93">Hat-based orchestration, planner-worker, passaggi umani e Gas Town sono confrontati come strutture di coordinamento con costi diversi.</data>
  <data key="d80">Più agenti non implicano più indipendenza né throughput lineare; integrazione, merge e capacità di revisione restano vincoli.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Human-agent collaboration", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:AI as reviewer", "K:Automation bias and trust", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C08", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "When to Scale Beyond Single Loops", "line": 20, "offset": 1643, "end": 1686}, {"level": "section", "title": "Human-in-the-Loop Patterns", "line": 277, "offset": 16282, "end": 16318}, {"level": "section", "title": "Understanding Gas Town (Conceptually)", "line": 500, "offset": 27527, "end": 27574}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Frontier: Evolutionary Software", "line": 624, "offset": 36444, "end": 36489}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
