<node id="B104">
  <data key="d73">Non-Deterministic Loop Engineering: A Critical Assessment</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V05</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Loop Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">NDLE/new_chapters/chapter01_foundations.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">bc900422e5a5ba75bc505fe8bc5cb5062604be18ffbad112f277c8367bd2f7d8</data>
  <data key="d365">1549</data>
  <data key="d366">8059</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V05/B104.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il loop affidabile emerge dall’interazione fra contesto, harness, evidenza e autorità.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il capitolo ricostruisce la genealogia prompt–loop, distingue worker ed evaluator, presenta livelli di delega e critica rischi sistemici e non-determinismo.</data>
  <data key="d80">I resoconti practitioner e le tassonomie di autonomia non stabiliscono frequenze di fallimento; separare ciò che è riportato dalle inferenze e dalle proposte dell’autore.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Engineering structure", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:AI as reviewer", "K:Automation bias and trust", "K:Specifications and governance", "K:Ownership and knowledge transfer", "K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Dependencies and agent supply chain"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C07", "C:C09", "C:C11"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "Introduction: The Epistemological Transition in Software Development", "line": 12, "offset": 795, "end": 873}, {"level": "section", "title": "From /loop to /goal : Native Loop Primitives", "line": 566, "offset": 24529, "end": 24600}, {"level": "section", "title": "Empirical Landscape: What Practitioners Actually Report", "line": 1071, "offset": 40241, "end": 40306}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Joint System: Context, Harness, Evidence, and Policy", "line": 1483, "offset": 59593, "end": 59659}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
