</node>
<node id="B108">
  <data key="d73">Building a Full Local AI Loop</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V05</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Loop Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">NDLE/new_chapters/chapter05_local_ai_loop.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">702b6ef3084dd35d95c15d7a44021b61a3ef7c556325541e0e433c983a7b9cb2</data>
  <data key="d365">1782</data>
  <data key="d366">10333</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V05/B108.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Un loop locale completo include runtime controllato, intenti durevoli, verifica e telemetria economica.</data>
  <data key="d93">Il percorso attraversa dimensionamento, energia e costo totale, installazione, scelta dell’executor, retry e resume, policy, osservabilità e gestione della deriva.</data>
  <data key="d80">La convenienza locale dipende da utilizzo, energia, ammortamento e tasso di accettazione. Installazioni e benchmark citati non sono stati rieseguiti; il titolo Start and Verify the Local Services ricorre due volte.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Economics</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Economics", "T:What agents can do", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory", "T:Productivity"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Economic costs and return", "K:Dependencies and agent supply chain", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Prompt injection and malicious tools", "K:Vulnerability and secure code", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale", "K:Output versus shipped value"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C06", "C:C07", "C:C09", "C:C12"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "The Decisive Shift: From Local Inference to Local Engineering", "line": 12, "offset": 650, "end": 721}, {"level": "section", "title": "Configuration as a Control Plane", "line": 816, "offset": 34881, "end": 34923}, {"level": "section", "title": "Loop Modes and Human Authority", "line": 1345, "offset": 59249, "end": 59289}, {"level": "section", "title": "The Durable Engineering Principles", "line": 1725, "offset": 81951, "end": 81995}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
  <data key="d375">NO</data>
  <data key="d95">ND.zip, 2026-10-11; original file retained unchanged</data>
</node>
<node id="B109">
  <data key="d73">Choosing the Right Loop</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V05</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Loop Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">NDLE/new_chapters/chapter06_choosing_the_right_loop.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">a061daf1e97a16c322a46cf9724dd0d92531718b57a038decdf521c6103f68b9</data>
  <data key="d365">1580</data>
  <data key="d366">10591</data>
  <data key="d367">chapter</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V05/B109.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Si sceglie il meccanismo minimo che affronta un fallimento osservato e dispone di un segnale esterno verificabile.</data>
  <data key="d93">Famiglie di tecniche, scala dell’evidenza, contratto del loop e decision framework culminano in un caso non-code di supporto clienti.</data>
  <data key="d80">La trasferibilità fra codice e assistenza clienti è una proposta di progetto; successo operativo, indipendenza del controllo e costo per esito richiedono valutazione nel dominio d’arrivo.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:Verification &amp; review</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:What agents can do", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Economics", "T:Productivity"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Human-agent collaboration", "K:Review capacity and maintainers", "K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Economic costs and return", "K:Output versus shipped value"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C07", "C:C08", "C:C11", "C:C12"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "section", "title": "From a Complete Architecture to a Selective Operating Model", "line": 12, "offset": 704, "end": 773}, {"level": "section", "title": "Technique Family IV: Budget, Observability, and Guardrails", "line": 628, "offset": 32214, "end": 32282}, {"level": "section", "title": "A Build Sequence That Minimizes Accidental Complexity", "line": 1163, "offset": 53964, "end": 54027}, {"level": "section", "title": "Conclusion: Engineering Accountable Autonomy", "line": 1565, "offset": 87266, "end": 87320}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
  <data key="d82">Author-authored engineering synthesis, guidance or reference apparatus</data>
  <data key="d374">File-level content mapping and citation-identity tracing; no independent validation or code execution</data>
