<node id="B111">
  <data key="d73">Glossary</data>
  <data key="d74">author_tex_section</data>
  <data key="d96">ND_INFORMATIONAL_TEX</data>
  <data key="d357">B</data>
  <data key="d358">V05</data>
  <data key="d363">Non-Deterministic Loop Engineering</data>
  <data key="d364">NDLE/glossary.tex</data>
  <data key="d356">39dbffdfcbff6363995d8c818eeaefeae1014ac01c26f98c3b5ab99f05ba86ef</data>
  <data key="d365">110</data>
  <data key="d366">1148</data>
  <data key="d367">glossary</data>
  <data key="d368">cards/V05/B111.md</data>
  <data key="d264">Il glossario stabilizza il significato di loop limitato, stato durevole, backpressure ed evidenza.</data>
  <data key="d93">Le definizioni separano segnale di completamento e prova, accettazione e stato provvisorio, capacità del modello e controlli del sistema.</data>
  <data key="d80">Una definizione è un vincolo terminologico interno, non una misura validata né un consenso universale della disciplina.</data>
  <data key="d369">T:What agents can do</data>
  <data key="d370">["T:What agents can do", "T:Verification &amp; review", "T:Engineering structure", "T:Code quality &amp; security", "T:System knowledge &amp; memory"]</data>
  <data key="d371">["K:Long-running agent execution", "K:Agent failure and escalation", "K:Independent verification and oracles", "K:Evaluation methodology and baselines", "K:Agent context and persistent memory", "K:System understanding and rationale"]</data>
  <data key="d372">["C:C03", "C:C07", "C:C09"]</data>
  <data key="d373">[{"level": "chapter", "title": "Glossary", "line": 1, "offset": 0, "end": 19}]</data>
  <data key="d362">Enrico Papalini</data>
