<node id="OCC:SDD2:A2">
  <data key="d73">Clarify Before Plan</data>
  <data key="d74">practice_occurrence</data>
  <data key="d357">OCC</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d378">F04</data>
  <data key="d383">Pattern A2</data>
  <data key="d355">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter15_patterns.tex</data>
  <data key="d384">91</data>
  <data key="d385">124</data>
  <data key="d356">4830546709bc5f2eb4641c47add3bb9992eb9089497514ac25f321b33f5f92aa</data>
  <data key="d386">["%  Sources: Spec Kit's clarification template; GSD's CLARIFY_BEFORE_PLAN rule.]", "\\paragraph{Practical example.} Tuesday at 10:14 Marta runs \\code{sdd new feat-042} followed by \\code{sdd run @clarification feat-042}. The agent returns seven questions: two P1 (``what is the PKCE \\code{code\\_verifier} lifetime?'' and ``does revocation cascade to issued ID tokens?''), four P2 (rate-limit ceiling, redirect-URI allow-list, log-retention horizon, device binding policy), one P3 (preferred clock source for token \\code{nbf}). Gate~1 stays closed until the security PO answers the two P1s; the four P2 assumptions are recorded in \\code{clarifications.md}. Gate~1 opens at 14:30, with the spec measurably less ambiguous than the version Marta would have shipped to \\code{@architect} unaided."]</data>
  <data key="d183">HISTORICAL_SOURCE_OCCURRENCE</data>
  <data key="d80">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
</node>
