<node id="OCC:SDD2:B4">
  <data key="d73">Convergence Review</data>
  <data key="d74">practice_occurrence</data>
  <data key="d357">OCC</data>
  <data key="d358">V03</data>
  <data key="d378">F08</data>
  <data key="d383">Pattern B4</data>
  <data key="d355">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter15_patterns.tex</data>
  <data key="d384">363</data>
  <data key="d385">399</data>
  <data key="d356">4830546709bc5f2eb4641c47add3bb9992eb9089497514ac25f321b33f5f92aa</data>
  <data key="d386">["%  during autonomous execution. Sources: multi-model debate pattern in advanced LLM research.]", "\\paragraph{Practical example.} Phase~2 of \\code{feat-042} reaches a fork: store the OAuth grant--token mapping as an \\textit{event-sourced} stream (every issue, refresh and revocation as an immutable event) or as a \\textit{state-based} table with an append-only audit shadow. Marta runs \\code{sdd gate check 2 --convergence}. The primary model proposes event-sourcing, citing audit fidelity; the second model challenges, pointing out that the merchant dashboard reads the current grant state on every checkout (4~ms p95 budget), and event-replay at that volume needs a snapshot strategy the team has not budgeted for. Synthesis: state-based table plus an append-only audit table for compliance --- the cheaper option that satisfies both the SLO and Article~4 audit requirement. Two-model latency: 8~minutes; durable rationale captured in \\code{plan.md} \\S4."]</data>
  <data key="d183">HISTORICAL_SOURCE_OCCURRENCE</data>
  <data key="d80">Attribution retained as written in the supplied source, not independently verified inventorship.</data>
</node>
