  <data key="d384">60</data>
  <data key="d385">67</data>
  <data key="d356">3c88f9e5d7b0288e46de69503668ac80ecb7778165d80bf74eab10da30c4e2ba</data>
  <data key="d386">["\\textbf{Ralph connection:} This is exactly the Planning Mode vs.\\ Building Mode distinction from \\chapref{ch:ralph}. Huntley's approach of using separate prompts for planning and building is an instance of this pattern. The key insight from the pattern catalogue is that the \\textit{plan itself should be treated as disposable}—regeneration is cheap, salvaging a corrupted plan is expensive."]</data>
