<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0115">
  <data key="d73">Xia and colleagues classified approximately 58\% of observed work as comprehension, including activity outside the editor. Chapter~\ref{chap:01} uses the author</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">15</data>
  <data key="d388">15</data>
  <data key="d389">Xia and colleagues classified approximately 58\% of observed work as comprehension, including activity outside the editor. Chapter~\ref{chap:01} uses the author-hosted manuscript\textquotesingle s 79 developers and 3,244 hours. The publication record uses 78 and 3,148, a version discrepancy retained in Appendix~\ref{app:methodology}; those populations should not be silently interchanged. The durable lesson is the breadth of comprehension work, not a universal time ratio or an estimate of agent savings. \autocite{W170}</data>
  <data key="d259">cd50635b07fc8c90e6d7407c65b6f9be8f2356029399e54ef5b1bc7bdb1c56f9</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W170"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0116">
  <data key="d73">\noindent\textbf{A brownfield permission map.} Osmani proposes green, yellow and red zones for mature repositories, assigned by people according to coverage, is</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">25</data>
  <data key="d388">25</data>
  <data key="d389">\noindent\textbf{A brownfield permission map.} Osmani proposes green, yellow and red zones for mature repositories, assigned by people according to coverage, isolation, institutional knowledge and potential consequences \osmanicite{O002}. The labels are useful as a provisional routing shorthand, not a numerical prediction of defect probability:</data>
  <data key="d259">1c9026541cb12065cd50cc8cb7a4ecd9bf23a66a1625d9c8eaea76e3b7ce6931</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O002"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0117">
  <data key="d73">Engineers maintain mental models of responsibilities, data flow, exceptional behavior and design rationale. LaToza, Venolia and DeLine\textquotesingle s explora</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">45</data>
  <data key="d388">45</data>
  <data key="d389">Engineers maintain mental models of responsibilities, data flow, exceptional behavior and design rationale. LaToza, Venolia and DeLine\textquotesingle s exploratory surveys and interviews describe the effort involved in recovering that knowledge within one corporation. Their self-selected observations motivate a design problem, rather than establish an effect of AI-mediated memory. \autocite{W186}</data>
  <data key="d259">9f3e239d531f90f78b8785602763f291d20aafe8795e24452a028948dca7ad79</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W186"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0118">
  <data key="d73">Ownership research uses contribution patterns as proxies for expertise and relates them to quality outcomes. Bird and colleagues found such associations in two </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">53</data>
  <data key="d388">53</data>
  <data key="d389">Ownership research uses contribution patterns as proxies for expertise and relates them to quality outcomes. Bird and colleagues found such associations in two Microsoft products; the study does not prove that changing ownership causally reduces defects. Wheeler\textquotesingle s argument that AI weakens authorship-based proxies is a separate conceptual claim. Together they invite scrutiny of the proxy, rather than a presumption that generated code is defective. \autocite{W182,W189}</data>
  <data key="d259">8fbb2bc8c191e3b51082fb16413686c00cf2f076da1e4683c2d3d979ed40d4d8</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W182", "W189"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0119">
  <data key="d73">A coding agent sees only the context it retrieves. Source files can be current while design notes are stale; tests may encode defects; summaries may omit author</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">61</data>
  <data key="d388">61</data>
  <data key="d389">A coding agent sees only the context it retrieves. Source files can be current while design notes are stale; tests may encode defects; summaries may omit authorization. The studies of contextual and conceptual pitfalls mapped to W155 and W158 motivate careful selection, without establishing a universal context recipe. More retrieved material is not necessarily more useful evidence. \autocite{W155,W158}</data>
  <data key="d259">326ee49d80d4c7ffdfbc38ff0aadbe314a2e77d7d1dea450094cfc08d7fb6e79</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W155", "W158"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0120">
  <data key="d73">An agent trace showing that nineteen tests passed is an episodic fact. It cannot prove that those tests cover the correct intention. A semantic card saying \tex</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">80</data>
  <data key="d388">80</data>
  <data key="d389">An agent trace showing that nineteen tests passed is an episodic fact. It cannot prove that those tests cover the correct intention. A semantic card saying \textquotesingle Treasury ceiling €3,000\textquotesingle{} is incomplete without its effective policy version. An intention contract has stronger authority about desired behavior, but it may not describe every implementation dependency. The memory mechanisms mapped to \autocite{W157}, \autocite{W159} and \autocite{W160} explore different representations and retrieval methods. \autocite{W157} is ClawVM, published at EuroMLSys 2026, DOI 10.1145/3805621.3807648, pp.~1--12, rather than merely an undated bibliography entry. It proposes harness-managed typed memory pages and validated writeback; its evaluation includes synthetic workloads, twelve real-session traces and adversarial tests. Those results concern state preservation under the authors\textquotesingle{} fault model, not demonstrated improvements in a software maintainer\textquotesingle s understanding. The empirical transfer of these mechanisms to brownfield comprehension remains to be established.</data>
  <data key="d259">b6260e0d9117aff907d58208849be2ea9aa41fe869be31901863e639e1ad9c92</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W157", "W159", "W160"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0121">
  <data key="d73">We therefore propose explicit memory states: CURRENT, SUPERSEDED, STALE\_BY\_INTENT\_DELTA, DISPUTED and UNKNOWN. Each record includes source, revision, validit</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">94</data>
  <data key="d388">94</data>
  <data key="d389">We therefore propose explicit memory states: CURRENT, SUPERSEDED, STALE\_BY\_INTENT\_DELTA, DISPUTED and UNKNOWN. Each record includes source, revision, validity scope, invalidation triggers and an accountable owner. These states are methodological proposals, not terminology empirically validated by \autocite{W157} or \autocite{W168}.</data>
  <data key="d259">6b5d2336d1e69c944ec2f13674050a07b127765b90acd5a3e050ac0cbdf3a35e</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W157", "W168"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0122">
  <data key="d73">\noindent\textbf{Renew context before reusing it.} Osmani treats context as an engineered selection of repository facts and constraints \osmanicite{O031}, shows</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">104</data>
  <data key="d388">104</data>
  <data key="d389">\noindent\textbf{Renew context before reusing it.} Osmani treats context as an engineered selection of repository facts and constraints \osmanicite{O031}, shows why long-running agents need durable handoff checkpoints \osmanicite{O013}, and recommends periodic audits of agent instruction files \osmanicite{O004}. Their practical synthesis for the approval service is a short renewal protocol. Before a new run, identify the context file's \emph{owner}, cite the source for each non-obvious invariant, record its \emph{intent revision and validity scope}, declare an \emph{expiry or invalidation trigger}, and keep procedural hints separate from tool permissions. Delete redundant instructions, quarantine retrieved text as data, and restart with an independently refreshed acceptance bundle when a material premise changes.</data>
  <data key="d259">0cb6dce9ba10fc57ecd980481442634f4b7953feb28f6e4b74a7c6694b830fc7</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O004", "O013", "O031"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0123">
  <data key="d73">Anokhin and colleagues\textquotesingle{} AriGraph combines semantic relations and episodic observations for agents. Its evaluated environments differ from softw</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">113</data>
  <data key="d388">113</data>
  <data key="d389">Anokhin and colleagues\textquotesingle{} AriGraph combines semantic relations and episodic observations for agents. Its evaluated environments differ from software maintenance, so it offers a representation mechanism rather than direct validation of this chapter\textquotesingle s handoff design. The IJCAI version and inspected locations are recorded in Appendix~\ref{app:methodology}. Our software graph still requires task-specific evaluation. \autocite{W160}</data>
  <data key="d259">456bc1f5d871ddef51a9f8dac6db070d1cfb9fbd1975f6902068396b4238de7c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W160"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0124">
  <data key="d73">Turnover exposes missing rationale: a repository may build while a successor cannot explain an exception or assess its removal. Mockus\textquotesingle{} histori</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">chapters/chapter09.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">125</data>
  <data key="d388">125</data>
  <data key="d389">Turnover exposes missing rationale: a repository may build while a successor cannot explain an exception or assess its removal. Mockus\textquotesingle{} historical succession study and Rigby and colleagues\textquotesingle{} file-based knowledge-loss analysis examine aspects of this problem. Their observational associations and repository-derived proxies do not estimate AI-assisted handover benefits. Appendix~\ref{app:methodology} preserves their distinct samples, numerical checks and remaining limitations. \autocite{W185,W173}</data>
  <data key="d259">36d04797717442f997b52793f5a0cefb2ad8addec35999c4c475260bf6ccb7ee</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W173", "W185"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
