<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0172">
  <data key="d73">The starting collection is \emph{The SE \&amp; AI Annotated Bibliography}, curated by Alfonso Fuggetta, Damian Andrew Tamburri and Alessandro Margara at \emph{Softw</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">15</data>
  <data key="d388">15</data>
  <data key="d389">The starting collection is \emph{The SE \&amp; AI Annotated Bibliography}, curated by Alfonso Fuggetta, Damian Andrew Tamburri and Alessandro Margara at \emph{Software Engineering @ PoliMi}. Its 193 works, organized into nine thematic streams, provide a broad map of research about AI and software engineering. The collection, original classifications and annotations belong to its curators; the engineering argument and teaching case in this book are a separate synthesis. \autocite{SEPolimiAnnotated2026}</data>
  <data key="d259">41ceb74278ea502d914a0353f8856972d6c3fb9ab64abb7dc0ead7a126aa1655</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["SEPolimiAnnotated2026"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="BIB:SEPolimiAnnotated2026">
  <data key="d73">The SE \&amp; AI Annotated Bibliography: 193 works on AI and software engineering, in nine streams</data>
  <data key="d74">auxiliary_bibliography</data>
  <data key="d357">AUX</data>
  <data key="d392">SEPolimiAnnotated2026</data>
  <data key="d78">https://www.sepolimi.com/p/se-ai-annotated-bibliography</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0173">
  <data key="d73">Three examples make the distinction concrete. An ambiguity score can direct attention to incomplete or conflicting statements, but the scoring dimensions, aggre</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">87</data>
  <data key="d388">87</data>
  <data key="d389">Three examples make the distinction concrete. An ambiguity score can direct attention to incomplete or conflicting statements, but the scoring dimensions, aggregation and decision threshold need their own evaluation. This book supplies no validated readiness score. A Convergence Review can reveal assumptions and competing reasons; agreement between its models is not an independent oracle. The general-model error research discussed in Chapter~\ref{chap:08} motivates examining dependence, but does not supply a coding-specific error rate for that review procedure. \autocite{W079}</data>
  <data key="d259">5f984bd353ae3f2083348c6c8d9e23a6e413387d26c63a856ffc7cb9b5c5350c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W079"]</data>
  <data key="d391">CHANGED_OR_NEW</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0174">
  <data key="d73">An Adversarial Agent changes the questions asked of the candidate, while a protected oracle changes which expectations the maker can alter. Those are different </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">89</data>
  <data key="d388">89</data>
  <data key="d389">An Adversarial Agent changes the questions asked of the candidate, while a protected oracle changes which expectations the maker can alter. Those are different properties. The buggy-code and self-review studies examined in Chapter~\ref{chap:07} illuminate particular programming failure modes; they do not validate every maker--checker arrangement. The local replay example instead demonstrates a narrower proposition: the deliberately wrong candidate passes its circular check and fails the independently specified stored-response check. Its file-broker and manifest tests concern the programmed permission and freshness predicates, not authenticated production authority. \autocite{W077,W101}</data>
  <data key="d259">ff99c5b5ef493dc02c90025727bf631031330e86dbda28fb7d2df7ef3a2bae8b</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W077", "W101"]</data>
  <data key="d391">CHANGED_OR_NEW</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0175">
  <data key="d73">Program-comprehension studies remind us that engineering includes reconstructing meaning before editing. Xia and colleagues observe professional work across too</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">99</data>
  <data key="d388">99</data>
  <data key="d389">Program-comprehension studies remind us that engineering includes reconstructing meaning before editing. Xia and colleagues observe professional work across tools; Minelli, Mocci and Lanza examine activity in a more specialized development environment. Their designs and populations differ, but both make understanding visible as work that a count of changed lines would miss. Neither study is an experiment on present-day coding agents. \autocite{W170,W176}</data>
  <data key="d259">0dc62875bb0cb5d269bc5ce0a5b4c90316d8e9aa203ab410dee489af55666adc</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W170", "W176"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0176">
  <data key="d73">Version details matter even for this familiar point. The author-hosted W170 manuscript describes 79 developers and 3,244 hours; the final version reports 78 and</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">101</data>
  <data key="d388">101</data>
  <data key="d389">Version details matter even for this familiar point. The author-hosted W170 manuscript describes 79 developers and 3,244 hours; the final version reports 78 and 3,148 after a participant's 96 hours were excluded. Some published project counts still total 79, and the retained activity shares have not been independently recomputed from the participant logs. The general observation that comprehension occupies substantial attention should therefore not be converted into an exact universal schedule for developers. \autocite{W170}</data>
  <data key="d259">2f9b8586c68bef590458ecda64e206f95c9699ea27e669a52287f007ac7940e3</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W170"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0177">
  <data key="d73">For the approval service, understanding why a historical decision must survive a policy change is part of the work, even when the implementation is only a few l</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">103</data>
  <data key="d388">103</data>
  <data key="d389">For the approval service, understanding why a historical decision must survive a policy change is part of the work, even when the implementation is only a few lines. Corporate rollout experiments such as W003 can measure output from introducing a coding assistant, but do not by themselves define whether that output is an operable business change. The book's broader work unit makes this remaining effort explicit; it is an engineering choice informed by the evidence. \autocite{W003}</data>
  <data key="d259">c595d783388818e8555915e7163bbbb689fdd6b3d657cd49951d73a2f4784ac2</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W003"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0178">
  <data key="d73">Cui and colleagues combine three company experiments involving 4,867 developers. The frequently cited pooled output estimate is not interchangeable with an esti</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">107</data>
  <data key="d388">107</data>
  <data key="d389">Cui and colleagues combine three company experiments involving 4,867 developers. The frequently cited pooled output estimate is not interchangeable with an estimate of assignment to treatment over a restricted period. Noncompliance and the distinction between assignment and actual use affect what is being estimated. Reading only a headline percentage would conceal those choices. \autocite{W003}</data>
  <data key="d259">31faffbee936e0f57b12eeec0834d33892e6a1714f95cf40e0bd63765fcb8ab4</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W003"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0179">
  <data key="d73">The experienced-maintainer experiment catalogued as W023 addresses a different setting. Its primary design involves sixteen developers and 246 issues, with rand</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">109</data>
  <data key="d388">109</data>
  <data key="d389">The experienced-maintainer experiment catalogued as W023 addresses a different setting. Its primary design involves sixteen developers and 246 issues, with random assignment at the issue level and developers working in both conditions. Its task-time result should be interpreted within that population, repository familiarity and tested tool setting, rather than treated as the answer to every productivity question. The contrast with a workplace rollout is informative precisely because the settings and endpoints differ. \autocite{W023}</data>
  <data key="d259">b64abe2a398f5fd3f50e315c2e23848fbc75865b202ff7d470de7b95f3ecbb57</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W023"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0180">
  <data key="d73">Enterprise surveys, broad practitioner surveys and vendor telemetry can explain adoption and perceived usefulness. They cannot substitute for timed work, review</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">111</data>
  <data key="d388">111</data>
  <data key="d389">Enterprise surveys, broad practitioner surveys and vendor telemetry can explain adoption and perceived usefulness. They cannot substitute for timed work, reviewer effort or post-release outcomes when those are the quantities a decision requires. Reports of confidence or speed belong beside the measured outcomes, with their own response denominator. \autocite{W007,W022,W021}</data>
  <data key="d259">1c756c61151d10702b35d94756db94b292c46250ad8e5979b648f2a4fe4be26e</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W007", "W021", "W022"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0181">
  <data key="d73">The AIDev dataset supports systematic examination of agent activity. Several publications reuse that corpus, including the analyses by Khelifi and colleagues an</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">119</data>
  <data key="d388">119</data>
  <data key="d389">The AIDev dataset supports systematic examination of agent activity. Several publications reuse that corpus, including the analyses by Khelifi and colleagues and by Peralta and colleagues. Their questions and samples differ, but the common lineage matters when assessing independent support. Peralta's review-trace sample and manually inspected subset are selections from an observed population, not fresh randomized trials. \autocite{W192,W068,W071}</data>
  <data key="d259">7acae949c93b25b557b21e7da566314523894092d8c556b7fd84b4c585446324</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W068", "W071", "W192"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0182">
  <data key="d73">MirrorCode explores longer-horizon task capability, while Whitfill and colleagues investigate why benchmark-passing patches may still fail maintainer expectatio</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">121</data>
  <data key="d388">121</data>
  <data key="d389">MirrorCode explores longer-horizon task capability, while Whitfill and colleagues investigate why benchmark-passing patches may still fail maintainer expectations. The latter assessment omits a normal iterative pull-request-and-CI cycle, so it does not estimate an actual production merge probability. Bhati's lifecycle synthesis, in turn, organizes earlier work rather than supplying another independently randomized sample. \autocite{W193,W111,W095}</data>
  <data key="d259">18f91119dfc0b3eaab573163176895727c192dfa7bb70998c65e4e144f9c0f34</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W095", "W111", "W193"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0183">
  <data key="d73">A test can be precise and still ask the wrong question. W148's simulated function-development processes illustrate this when an articulated requirement and a na</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">127</data>
  <data key="d388">127</data>
  <data key="d389">A test can be precise and still ask the wrong question. W148's simulated function-development processes illustrate this when an articulated requirement and a narrower supplied oracle disagree. A candidate may satisfy one interpretation and fail the other. The lesson is to inspect the authority behind the expected result, not merely count passing cases. \autocite{W148}</data>
  <data key="d259">14033416a91071e1b272089571c59f1c7bf4e3d8cce1c870c7344624a79c986d</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W148"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0184">
  <data key="d73">Intent-prediction and drift-scoring work such as W099 examines the effort involved in keeping model behavior aligned with a changing requirement. Its scoring co</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">129</data>
  <data key="d388">129</data>
  <data key="d389">Intent-prediction and drift-scoring work such as W099 examines the effort involved in keeping model behavior aligned with a changing requirement. Its scoring costs and nonrandomized rollout do not establish a universally effective retry rule or an automated authority for deciding intention. Process proposals by Hassan and Hoda offer useful ways to organize responsibilities, while the repository-policy study W150 records written obligations rather than runtime compliance. \autocite{W099,W152,W153,W150}</data>
  <data key="d259">95e2c274a81bcd14281de56dbbaf9550c0b02f884aea1de8fae76db421635e6c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W099", "W150", "W152", "W153"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0185">
  <data key="d73">The benchmark changes between versions of W151 also constrain what can be inferred from its results. An earlier edition describes $\tau$-bench; a later edition </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">131</data>
  <data key="d388">131</data>
  <data key="d389">The benchmark changes between versions of W151 also constrain what can be inferred from its results. An earlier edition describes $\tau$-bench; a later edition uses a TravelPlanner constraint task. Those headlines are not repeated measurements on an unchanged benchmark. Some reported seed summaries also lack the observations and endpoint definitions needed for reconciliation. The control ideas can be discussed without treating those unresolved comparisons as validated performance estimates. \autocite{W151}</data>
  <data key="d259">2969046087391b8885738955042c63860f1154084101dac49eb747790f6d4d51</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W151"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0186">
  <data key="d73">A change can pass its immediate tests while making the next change harder. Observational studies of agent-first and IDE-first repositories, and of Cursor adopti</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">137</data>
  <data key="d388">137</data>
  <data key="d389">A change can pass its immediate tests while making the next change harder. Observational studies of agent-first and IDE-first repositories, and of Cursor adoption, examine this possibility through activity, complexity and static-analysis measures. W001 distinguishes its repository groups rather than estimating a single pooled ``39\%'' complexity effect. W004's quality results also vary materially with estimator choice: an alternative specification gives negative, statistically insignificant estimates where the preferred one reports increases. These are reasons to investigate maintainability, not to declare a tool universally harmful. \autocite{W001,W004}</data>
  <data key="d259">eae9be10f9eb12d792f3adb89c0d8adfac074ad07085e0d456623060168c879c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W001", "W004"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0187">
  <data key="d73">Redundancy adds another perspective. Huang and colleagues report a higher redundancy measure for agentic pull requests alongside relatively favorable review-com</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">139</data>
  <data key="d388">139</data>
  <data key="d389">Redundancy adds another perspective. Huang and colleagues report a higher redundancy measure for agentic pull requests alongside relatively favorable review-comment sentiment. That combination can motivate a check for missed reuse, but the sentiment classifier does not establish what a reviewer understood. A discrepancy between the complexity-table total and the surrounding reported count further limits precise reuse of that table; it does not erase the separately reported redundancy comparison. \autocite{W031}</data>
  <data key="d259">ad099496678c74cf15c96ba50977ff5c459728f2cbd5447326e2b7af5433d567</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W031"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0188">
  <data key="d73">Post-merge studies help distinguish a warning from work that actually follows. W029 reports introduced SonarQube issues in merged Python bug fixes, with highly </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">141</data>
  <data key="d388">141</data>
  <data key="d389">Post-merge studies help distinguish a warning from work that actually follows. W029 reports introduced SonarQube issues in merged Python bug fixes, with highly unequal agent-group sizes and concentrated findings. W054 follows changes over ninety days and examines outcomes including reverts. A raw vendor total, an issue-presence test, an issue-density test and a revert comparison answer different questions. Reconstructing the approximate revert odds ratios from rounded published percentages checks that arithmetic, not the original model or its handling of selection. \autocite{W029,W054}</data>
  <data key="d259">621cbefa66a064c4cababd365541bfef925b5935ff44576d6eea0b6b5b33cace</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W029", "W054"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0189">
  <data key="d73">The practical response is to keep architecture and maintenance evidence separate from a passing test. A duplicated Treasury threshold imposes a synchronization </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">143</data>
  <data key="d388">143</data>
  <data key="d389">The practical response is to keep architecture and maintenance evidence separate from a passing test. A duplicated Treasury threshold imposes a synchronization obligation even when its cyclomatic complexity is low. Authorship and ownership records may identify a steward, but do not prove that the steward can diagnose and safely revise the behavior. An explicit handoff and a change-focused fitness check address that gap. \autocite{W189}</data>
  <data key="d259">5bb82ecb34b064f9d049de96762d61bce782cca41a7d007fa8d10546063a45da</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W189"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0190">
  <data key="d73">The often-repeated 45\% failure figure in W061 concerns eighty constructed tasks under the tested models and judging procedure. Schreiber and Tippe instead iden</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">149</data>
  <data key="d388">149</data>
  <data key="d389">The often-repeated 45\% failure figure in W061 concerns eighty constructed tasks under the tested models and judging procedure. Schreiber and Tippe instead identify publicly attributed AI code through GitHub searches and successive filtering, then examine patterns reported by CodeQL. Attribution comments are unevenly used, and detected patterns are not verified exploits. Neither design supplies the base rate of exploitable flaws in an arbitrary deployed organization. \autocite{W061,W041}</data>
  <data key="d259">191af58d7958aaff711d6f2d523335fcdd1b462119ca84dd077981f0babf0656</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W041", "W061"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0191">
  <data key="d73">A written contribution policy can require review without demonstrating that a runtime prevents secret reads, network actions or direct merges. The selected repo</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">151</data>
  <data key="d388">151</data>
  <data key="d389">A written contribution policy can require review without demonstrating that a runtime prevents secret reads, network actions or direct merges. The selected repository policies in W150 illuminate governance language, not enforcement of those boundaries. \autocite{W150}</data>
  <data key="d259">d2f2b1a492129e0329c905b7f42d3edb929d8ecd25213594d4978ec5231081a3</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W150"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0192">
  <data key="d73">Independence concerns where an expected answer comes from. A second model can repeat the first model's mistake, especially when both share incomplete context or</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">157</data>
  <data key="d388">157</data>
  <data key="d389">Independence concerns where an expected answer comes from. A second model can repeat the first model's mistake, especially when both share incomplete context or related failure patterns. W079's conditional agreement result concerns multiple-choice answers when both models are wrong. It motivates caution about consensus, but is not an overall coding-agent failure rate. W148's oracle anomalies and W111's maintainer judgments make the complementary point that even executable correctness can be narrower than the acceptance question. \autocite{W079,W148,W111}</data>
  <data key="d259">8141e381773e597b1f4f5dbeb7a572bbddf6eefe69bf78c0cf7ce0424b3ebc4c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W079", "W111", "W148"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0193">
  <data key="d73">Xiang and colleagues evaluate writer/reviewer combinations on the same 116 complete-case programming tasks. The reviewing models cannot run the tests that later</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">159</data>
  <data key="d388">159</data>
  <data key="d389">Xiang and colleagues evaluate writer/reviewer combinations on the same 116 complete-case programming tasks. The reviewing models cannot run the tests that later score correctness. In that setting, reviewer order matters: one sequence adds passing tasks to its writer-only baseline, while the reverse loses successes and costs more. Reconstructed McNemar calculations use the published discordant counts, not independently rerun model outputs. The result illustrates why another review stage needs evaluation; it does not establish an optimal brownfield review process. \autocite{W102}</data>
  <data key="d259">04f2533572dcfb2b70f24cd0b5dcf713648f62fcff1b3fe165169887adb619d2</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W102"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0194">
  <data key="d73">Statistical checks have an oracle problem of their own. W151 reports a difference in mean constraint satisfaction and invokes a paired McNemar test without the </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">161</data>
  <data key="d388">161</data>
  <data key="d389">Statistical checks have an oracle problem of their own. W151 reports a difference in mean constraint satisfaction and invokes a paired McNemar test without the categorical discordance table needed to reproduce it. Means alone do not determine those paired outcomes. A plausible reconstruction must therefore remain a hypothesis until the relevant observations are available. \autocite{W151}</data>
  <data key="d259">7ee5197a8b3ecf0100c0bd7d56a2e5f3fac5d22bcbbd760b93ad59c879d3552b</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W151"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0195">
  <data key="d73">Human-review studies can likewise measure trust, agreement and time without measuring escaped production defects. Those outcomes matter, but cannot certify the </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">163</data>
  <data key="d388">163</data>
  <data key="d389">Human-review studies can likewise measure trust, agreement and time without measuring escaped production defects. Those outcomes matter, but cannot certify the service's release. Its checker needs an expectation grounded in the authorized contract and evidence tied to a particular candidate. \autocite{W066}</data>
  <data key="d259">b0da2097aec80cb7efce721bc0cc60bb190e17d767d9460ff183911e1e862379</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W066"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0196">
  <data key="d73">Watanabe and colleagues describe 567 Claude Code pull requests across 157 projects, including merge and modification patterns. Other studies examine interventio</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">169</data>
  <data key="d388">169</data>
  <data key="d389">Watanabe and colleagues describe 567 Claude Code pull requests across 157 projects, including merge and modification patterns. Other studies examine intervention, review context and reasons for rejection. Peralta's manually inspected rejected cases distinguish agentic failures, non-agentic workflow causes and unknown reasons. The sample is stratified, and missing traces can hide work. These classifications describe what was observable; they are not a population-wide estimate of how often humans should intervene. \autocite{W036,W068,W065,W071}</data>
  <data key="d259">d3cacabfd4767c76a8349814b1dfc5a78751a5d14a0fdce157afce59c67c092b</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W036", "W065", "W068", "W071"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0197">
  <data key="d73">Counting also requires care. W072's same-product and cross-product review groups overlap, so summing them overcounts distinct pull requests. W068 has an unresol</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">171</data>
  <data key="d388">171</data>
  <data key="d389">Counting also requires care. W072's same-product and cross-product review groups overlap, so summing them overcounts distinct pull requests. W068 has an unresolved discrepancy between a table's category total and its stated overall count. An arithmetically plausible replacement cell does not become a corrected observation without the underlying records. \autocite{W072,W068}</data>
  <data key="d259">4f687e439e9345b2aaf5a8ec458ff0d4414571cc8e7e3d1cdea89b62b4b5fc5b</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W068", "W072"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0198">
  <data key="d73">Automation-bias research offers mechanisms for understanding over-reliance on advice, but its adjacent settings do not supply a safe software-review threshold. </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">173</data>
  <data key="d388">173</data>
  <data key="d389">Automation-bias research offers mechanisms for understanding over-reliance on advice, but its adjacent settings do not supply a safe software-review threshold. Intent scoring introduces its own costs, and a self-selected rollout cannot isolate its deployment benefit. \autocite{W085,W087,W099}</data>
  <data key="d259">075e1d8730110c00be921851df44b2204fff6cfd4976de6efbb04472ae4bb4a1</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W085", "W087", "W099"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0199">
  <data key="d73">A repository preserves code more readily than the reasoning that shaped it. Comprehension research, industrial ownership succession and discussions of generated</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">179</data>
  <data key="d388">179</data>
  <data key="d389">A repository preserves code more readily than the reasoning that shaped it. Comprehension research, industrial ownership succession and discussions of generated-code authorship all suggest different ways of examining that problem. They do not establish that one graph format, memory store or AI-generated summary improves the next maintainer's performance. \autocite{W170,W185,W189}</data>
  <data key="d259">9aa79b6c82dd13d3a6585fa7f4965f70674f94a25de11b842b9fc11d4978b215</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W170", "W185", "W189"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0200">
  <data key="d73">Completing an assisted task is not the same observation as explaining it unaided or applying the lesson later. The main W118 experiment assesses participants im</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">187</data>
  <data key="d388">187</data>
  <data key="d389">Completing an assisted task is not the same observation as explaining it unaided or applying the lesson later. The main W118 experiment assesses participants immediately after work with a new library. Its six usage-pattern groups are exploratory rather than randomly assigned teaching strategies. Figure~\ref{fig:ch10-research-2} accordingly shows an immediate quiz comparison, not delayed retention. \autocite{W118}</data>
  <data key="d259">0e6138bc0f618246297a2a0963f5471e88211d079a812a7acc67b116116d214e</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W118"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0201">
  <data key="d73">An unresolved reporting detail makes restraint especially important. The source reports a 4.15-point difference on a 27-point quiz while describing a 17\% diffe</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">189</data>
  <data key="d388">189</data>
  <data key="d389">An unresolved reporting detail makes restraint especially important. The source reports a 4.15-point difference on a 27-point quiz while describing a 17\% difference. Dividing the stated quantities does not reproduce that summary, and a different normalization cannot be assumed. The book therefore retains the reported direction of the immediate comparison without presenting a corrected relative skill-loss percentage. Participant-level observations and the intended calculation would be needed to settle it. \autocite{W118}</data>
  <data key="d259">99369ff61a21cb4a119fd68834a6fea077e62f1c4afae604e64d3afad0ec1228</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W118"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0202">
  <data key="d73">Ide's knowledge-transmission model asks a different question. Novices learn tacit knowledge through work with experienced people; changing which tasks they perf</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">191</data>
  <data key="d388">191</data>
  <data key="d389">Ide's knowledge-transmission model asks a different question. Novices learn tacit knowledge through work with experienced people; changing which tasks they perform can alter future learning even when current output rises. That is a theoretical mechanism under specified assumptions, not a measured fall in developers' skills or employment. Earlier illustrative growth scenarios should not be attributed to a later version's result, and the versioned PDF is the fixed source where renderings disagree. \autocite{W120}</data>
  <data key="d259">366f2dabe3261e1f6a2155236a0f0404016fe7c326e9c1dff85c32eb0a8dc940</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W120"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0203">
  <data key="d73">Historical work on onboarding, comprehension and novice learning supplies additional perspectives, with different participants, tasks, instruments and intervals</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">193</data>
  <data key="d388">193</data>
  <data key="d389">Historical work on onboarding, comprehension and novice learning supplies additional perspectives, with different participants, tasks, instruments and intervals before assessment. Those differences matter as much as the tool used during the task. \autocite{W115,W161,W163,W164,W166,W167,W169,W170}</data>
  <data key="d259">81167e31e3129c1431145ff835e94eb8996df514ab4abe16975e16a8f8612faf</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W115", "W161", "W163", "W164", "W166", "W167", "W169", "W170"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0204">
  <data key="d73">A policy survey tells us what a set of organizations has written. It does not tell us whether the policy is enforced, whether a tool cannot bypass it, or whethe</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">199</data>
  <data key="d388">199</data>
  <data key="d389">A policy survey tells us what a set of organizations has written. It does not tell us whether the policy is enforced, whether a tool cannot bypass it, or whether its use improves delivery. W150 combines 245 policies found among 2,000 repositories with 36 deliberately added organizations. Results for that enriched sample should not be described as the prevalence of a practice across all repositories. Without the extra organizations' labels, even the corresponding discovered-policy rate cannot be recovered exactly. \autocite{W150}</data>
  <data key="d259">92404a31e3738aab93d887f965e2537513c2f00f40a88f8115d7d935e6462f7f</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W150"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0205">
  <data key="d73">Conceptual process proposals and simulated function-building studies contribute other kinds of insight. Their roles, coordination patterns and measured endpoint</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">201</data>
  <data key="d388">201</data>
  <data key="d389">Conceptual process proposals and simulated function-building studies contribute other kinds of insight. Their roles, coordination patterns and measured endpoints cannot be pooled into a governance-effect estimate. The operating model in this book instead makes ownership, evidence freshness, conflict resolution and release authority explicit so those controls can be examined in a real workflow. \autocite{W152,W153,W148}</data>
  <data key="d259">4d11137f807422367e5d530ac07f2ab32b6b9d4eb72b435cf4268bd209cc5185</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W148", "W152", "W153"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0206">
  <data key="d73">Organizational return claims need similar separation. Surveys and vendor material may contain reported benefits with self-selected denominators. The McKinsey ex</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">203</data>
  <data key="d388">203</data>
  <data key="d389">Organizational return claims need similar separation. Surveys and vendor material may contain reported benefits with self-selected denominators. The McKinsey excerpt catalogued as W028 combines a bank case, potential leverage scenarios and a reference to a separate company analysis; its twentyfold frontier scenario is not an observed mean across that company sample. DORA's return-on-investment guidance and calculator are decision aids, not randomized demonstrations of a fixed return. \autocite{W026,W024,W028,W145}</data>
  <data key="d259">99f4ec12999ffa9327b5ddd146bc4a04758677949529f8e09a74f3accf8f648f</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W024", "W026", "W028", "W145"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0207">
  <data key="d73">The economic question is broader than whether a tool produces more code. Corporate output experiments, platform studies and labor-market analyses observe differ</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">209</data>
  <data key="d388">209</data>
  <data key="d389">The economic question is broader than whether a tool produces more code. Corporate output experiments, platform studies and labor-market analyses observe different populations and endpoints. W003's output measure, W010's version-dependent platform estimates and W136's labor-market findings cannot be combined into a single accepted-change cost. Pre-adoption earnings differences are not treatment effects, and confidence bounds from different specifications are not interchangeable. \autocite{W003,W010,W136}</data>
  <data key="d259">67f89bfa17e7832f5132e5acdb2caf337b29a4709c86d7666860c44bac1f2bd9</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W003", "W010", "W136"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0208">
  <data key="d73">Workforce interpretation is particularly sensitive to the denominator. In Chandar and Klein Teeselink's analytic sample, a lower junior share is associated prim</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">211</data>
  <data key="d388">211</data>
  <data key="d389">Workforce interpretation is particularly sensitive to the denominator. In Chandar and Klein Teeselink's analytic sample, a lower junior share is associated primarily with higher senior employment; the estimated junior-headcount reduction is not statistically significant. The matched-affiliate analysis is narrower than the large underlying postings and employment datasets, and its adoption measure and identification assumptions limit causal interpretation. A falling share is not, by itself, a measured decline in the total number of young workers. \autocite{W126}</data>
  <data key="d259">be893f65f1b366f9a7b768aa83fb73ad7558a32a0b3d9999fe6101167808bc46</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W126"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0209">
  <data key="d73">Vacancies, employment, wages, occupational shares and firm spending remain separate outcomes. Forecasts and competing interpretations can help identify scenario</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">213</data>
  <data key="d388">213</data>
  <data key="d389">Vacancies, employment, wages, occupational shares and firm spending remain separate outcomes. Forecasts and competing interpretations can help identify scenarios, but hiring cycles, remote work and capital constraints are alternative explanations that require appropriate designs. They should remain visible when discussing AI's possible contribution. \autocite{W019,W025,W127,W135,W138,W130,W142}</data>
  <data key="d259">cfcc5c93566157f7ea7165d6ba685163b0d1740cbf9a690d27bb9186851b9841</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W019", "W025", "W127", "W130", "W135", "W138", "W142"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0210">
  <data key="d73">The \emph{70\% problem} and the discussion of apparently finished work make the gap between generation and delivery memorable. Their value is to draw attention </data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">221</data>
  <data key="d388">221</data>
  <data key="d389">The \emph{70\% problem} and the discussion of apparently finished work make the gap between generation and delivery memorable. Their value is to draw attention to the remaining integration, review and rework, not to establish a measured completion percentage. The book uses that distinction to ask what an accepted change actually costs. \osmanicite{O049,O029}</data>
  <data key="d259">251c193127b3c5b5a47cb6ef24dc37440449bdd05162a5e363a647031734a878</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O029", "O049"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0211">
  <data key="d73">Agency and orchestration describe different choices. One agent can have consequential authority in a single workspace, while a team of read-only agents can requ</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">225</data>
  <data key="d388">225</data>
  <data key="d389">Agency and orchestration describe different choices. One agent can have consequential authority in a single workspace, while a team of read-only agents can require coordination without permission to alter policy. Osmani's illustrative autonomy levels help name possible arrangements, but do not constitute a validated maturity scale. \osmanicite{O010}</data>
  <data key="d259">b9f99abd43e625a53a13f4a61575e3ed932802794aca727fd006041043ea69b3</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O010"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0212">
  <data key="d73">Loop mechanisms make some of the responsibilities concrete: scheduling, isolated work, versioned procedures, governed connectors, specialist tasks and durable p</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">227</data>
  <data key="d388">227</data>
  <data key="d389">Loop mechanisms make some of the responsibilities concrete: scheduling, isolated work, versioned procedures, governed connectors, specialist tasks and durable progress state. Their presence should make the work easier to observe and bound. A specialist subagent is not independent merely because it has a separate name, and a stopped loop has not thereby earned release permission. \osmanicite{O012,O006}</data>
  <data key="d259">1acd6ec43ad4996d501fec64a0dc35112149772bfa26f00996bc89d831379177</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O006", "O012"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0213">
  <data key="d73">The same distinction applies to specifications. A well-formed machine-authored contract can be an excellent proposal while still lacking authorization. Osmani's</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">229</data>
  <data key="d388">229</data>
  <data key="d389">The same distinction applies to specifications. A well-formed machine-authored contract can be an excellent proposal while still lacking authorization. Osmani's specification guidance helps make a task explicit; the policy owner remains responsible for its business meaning. In the approval service, a late Treasury revision requires that decision before the model is asked to implement it. \osmanicite{O018,O028}</data>
  <data key="d259">c0a2be4d5e352608c810b563b59dd5523b940b973e46562e83d601cdf60c417d</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O018", "O028"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0214">
  <data key="d73">The recommendation to treat generated code as a draft and the later discussion of code nobody can fully read address a changing review burden. They are more use</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">233</data>
  <data key="d388">233</data>
  <data key="d389">The recommendation to treat generated code as a draft and the later discussion of code nobody can fully read address a changing review burden. They are more useful as a tension to resolve than as opposing universal rules. A bounded change can rely on strong independent checks, while a high-impact change still needs appropriate domain judgment and accountable acceptance. Neither essay supplies a universally safe proportion of code that humans may stop inspecting. \osmanicite{O023,O001}</data>
  <data key="d259">6713c5a7a65d07e301836b21d4406a8020347aa6c91c3b665276d517119913e2</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O001", "O023"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0215">
  <data key="d73">Brownfield delegation and context management extend the responsibility beyond a single run. A change zone, instruction file or checkpoint can preserve useful in</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">235</data>
  <data key="d388">235</data>
  <data key="d389">Brownfield delegation and context management extend the responsibility beyond a single run. A change zone, instruction file or checkpoint can preserve useful information, but can also preserve a stale assumption. Version, owner, source and invalidation conditions make that information usable without silently promoting a summary into authority. The memory arrangement then needs a handoff test, not merely successful retrieval. \osmanicite{O002,O031,O013,O004}</data>
  <data key="d259">df63306b391b4bf42713f8ef781056ac4329b72fd16c98c7941159c1e40d77ab</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O002", "O004", "O013", "O031"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0216">
  <data key="d73">Warnings about agentic skill decay and the \emph{80\% problem} bring the engineer back into view. They raise questions about lost practice, comprehension and re</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">237</data>
  <data key="d388">237</data>
  <data key="d389">Warnings about agentic skill decay and the \emph{80\% problem} bring the engineer back into view. They raise questions about lost practice, comprehension and responsibility rather than provide population estimates of competence. The proposed delayed-transfer evaluation is one way to investigate those concerns without assuming their conclusion. \osmanicite{O003,O017}</data>
  <data key="d259">d37d9eb72ee0991ee38c204f69618c028a192f1a049e6b4028e8b298b9ab4fcf</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O003", "O017"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0217">
  <data key="d73">``Own the outer loop'' connects these themes. People remain responsible for intention, evaluation design, escalation and operational consequences while delegati</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">239</data>
  <data key="d388">239</data>
  <data key="d389">``Own the outer loop'' connects these themes. People remain responsible for intention, evaluation design, escalation and operational consequences while delegating bounded inner work. That prescription is a useful basis for designing responsibilities; its value should be judged through the actual effort, releases, incidents and learning it enables. \osmanicite{O009}</data>
  <data key="d259">f36a3e432e6e66c09c9bd0c31833660675d16f58e875ff4fa8ca94ad5c74154a</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["O009"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0218">
  <data key="d73">Orosz and Laura Tacho's measurement discussion connects tool adoption with delivery, quality and developer experience. It motivates the book's measurement-to-de</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">247</data>
  <data key="d388">247</data>
  <data key="d389">Orosz and Laura Tacho's measurement discussion connects tool adoption with delivery, quality and developer experience. It motivates the book's measurement-to-decision table, without validating that proposed instrument or supplying the approval service's acceptance probabilities. At publication, the article disclosed Orosz's investment in DX, Tacho's role there and that the article was not sponsored. Those relationships accompany the reported practices and should remain part of their interpretation. \oroszcite{P061}</data>
  <data key="d259">513a2843f32a780f82e2e5436f6fed5f6f6e60c58c6d80e26d98b2fd61e669e6</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P061"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0219">
  <data key="d73">The discussion of loop engineering supplies a useful challenge to Osmani's vocabulary: does the additional coordinator still earn its complexity when existing t</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">249</data>
  <data key="d388">249</data>
  <data key="d389">The discussion of loop engineering supplies a useful challenge to Osmani's vocabulary: does the additional coordinator still earn its complexity when existing tooling can provide some mechanisms? This concerns implementation, not the disappearance of engineering responsibilities. The article discusses the underlying Osmani work through another edition; it is neither independent confirmation of that work nor a universal refutation of controlled loops. \oroszcite{P110}</data>
  <data key="d259">af2fc7bd32426a30105144cb1985d75214676931eee88b9fa40d53e041315efb</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P110"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0220">
  <data key="d73">Drew Hoskins's diagnostic-design excerpt, introduced through Orosz's interview, helps explain why an error message is part of behavior rather than decoration. A</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">255</data>
  <data key="d388">255</data>
  <data key="d389">Drew Hoskins's diagnostic-design excerpt, introduced through Orosz's interview, helps explain why an error message is part of behavior rather than decoration. A conflict should identify the condition and a permitted next step. It should not encourage a caller to overwrite a historical decision or evade policy by retrying with a new key. The diagnostic contract in the exercise is this book's adaptation of that guidance. \oroszcite{P082}</data>
  <data key="d259">312c606b90c72221d185d485bca0abdb83f3145baf27dfedcd561f27834f0a86</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P082"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0221">
  <data key="d73">Orosz and Elin Nilsson's Antithesis report offers a related debugging lesson: preserve the conditions that make a failure reproducible. Its company account does</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">257</data>
  <data key="d388">257</data>
  <data key="d389">Orosz and Elin Nilsson's Antithesis report offers a related debugging lesson: preserve the conditions that make a failure reproducible. Its company account does not turn the book's lost-response pseudocode into an executed simulator, and deterministic repetition still does not establish that the oracle is correct. A later free-access or sponsorship notice also remains separate from the original article's publication context. \oroszcite{P006}</data>
  <data key="d259">bfa3c9ff6aebbc0eabdeff2f69f80eedc721f6c315b9227b837265edef213f3a</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P006"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0222">
  <data key="d73">The visible discussion of code-review practice sharpens another distinction. A human can resolve every model comment while an important obligation remains untes</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">259</data>
  <data key="d388">259</data>
  <data key="d389">The visible discussion of code-review practice sharpens another distinction. A human can resolve every model comment while an important obligation remains untested. The proposed coverage ledger therefore asks what evidence supports historical replay, not just whether the reviewer has anything left to say. Reported company practices do not supply a universal release policy. \oroszcite{P118}</data>
  <data key="d259">568bc68b10c0adb73fd314f10c24afa8e8364609e5ae7d070b9ed6910a52c00c</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P118"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0223">
  <data key="d73">Kent Beck's optimistic discussion of AI as a learning amplifier provides a counter-hypothesis to lost practice. In the edited panel, Orosz is the credited autho</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">263</data>
  <data key="d388">263</data>
  <data key="d389">Kent Beck's optimistic discussion of AI as a learning amplifier provides a counter-hypothesis to lost practice. In the edited panel, Orosz is the credited author and moderator; Beck and Martin Fowler are participants. Their interpretation motivates a question, not a measured effect. The book's two assisted-work conditions test structured practice and cannot establish AI's total effect by comparison with an unassisted group. \oroszcite{P123}</data>
  <data key="d259">ba6f622a62949ecb9861a0dff75db0ff8de6c00ebb0887d6f09311255debf596</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P123"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0224">
  <data key="d73">Nicole Forsgren and Abi Noda's \emph{Frictionless} excerpts, introduced through Orosz's interview, focus attention on the conditions in which engineers work. Th</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">265</data>
  <data key="d388">265</data>
  <data key="d389">Nicole Forsgren and Abi Noda's \emph{Frictionless} excerpts, introduced through Orosz's interview, focus attention on the conditions in which engineers work. The useful transfer is to distinguish repeated preparation and missing evidence from the assurance work and policy decisions a team genuinely needs. Improving how a control is performed is different from deleting its purpose. \oroszcite{P078}</data>
  <data key="d259">2434f546b8ddad6c06b144c29861c6056c93b33854bf96d27849e3e52fdc36fb</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P078"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0225">
  <data key="d73">The economic examples close the circle. Orosz's personal replacement of a small service and his Simon Eskildsen interview about rough resource reasoning encoura</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">267</data>
  <data key="d388">267</data>
  <data key="d389">The economic examples close the circle. Orosz's personal replacement of a small service and his Simon Eskildsen interview about rough resource reasoning encourage scrutiny of scope and assumptions. A quick implementation does not include all the obligations of maintaining an equivalent service. Rough bounds can identify what should be measured; a headline build time or reported saving cannot become a local model coefficient. \oroszcite{P084,P111}</data>
  <data key="d259">d5b4946c40e3ad53ccc1e66ad2fbb445e61df3aeba080d09090912c7d40e7035</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P084", "P111"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0226">
  <data key="d73">Publication count can exaggerate independent support. P014 is an edited republication of Osmani's O049 with added commentary. Its second publication does not cr</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">271</data>
  <data key="d388">271</data>
  <data key="d389">Publication count can exaggerate independent support. P014 is an edited republication of Osmani's O049 with added commentary. Its second publication does not create a second observation. P052 reports the experiment already catalogued as W023; the primary sixteen-developer, 246-issue, issue-randomized design remains authoritative where the secondary description differs. \oroszcite{P014,P052}</data>
  <data key="d259">09fb59e7e927bd9e803101d1ff9a4fe671cef140ac3abf65c4844057756c8058</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P014", "P052"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0227">
  <data key="d73">Similarly, P089, P095 and P101 analyze one voluntary reader cohort. Distinct questions justify distinct articles, but not three independent samples or a matched</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">273</data>
  <data key="d388">273</data>
  <data key="d389">Similarly, P089, P095 and P101 analyze one voluntary reader cohort. Distinct questions justify distinct articles, but not three independent samples or a matched longitudinal panel. The survey can contain primary descriptive observations without establishing causation or population-wide effects. Overlapping Summit context also limits the independence of related panel reporting. \oroszcite{P089,P095,P101}</data>
  <data key="d259">68743a2972afcfac2065d2464ff70a471c10118adfdd48283978e02b1be332f7</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["P089", "P095", "P101"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0228">
  <data key="d73">Some remaining questions require original observations. W003's estimators need the underlying assignment and task records for an independent refit. W068's discr</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">281</data>
  <data key="d388">281</data>
  <data key="d389">Some remaining questions require original observations. W003's estimators need the underlying assignment and task records for an independent refit. W068's discrepant table count needs matched repository records rather than an inferred replacement. W170's retained activity shares require participant logs to reconcile them. Until those materials are analyzed, the book keeps the affected interpretations qualified. \autocite{W003,W068,W170}</data>
  <data key="d259">d3dd3fac1044e0835a973a5e0910148f199a3a54b00f996eca9d2c8dd33869cc</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W003", "W068", "W170"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0229">
  <data key="d73">Other questions concern the connection between a model or instrument and the world. W120's theoretical assumptions need to be examined separately from real know</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/methodology.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">283</data>
  <data key="d388">283</data>
  <data key="d389">Other questions concern the connection between a model or instrument and the world. W120's theoretical assumptions need to be examined separately from real knowledge transfer. W150's original policy classifications need independent inspection before a stronger coding-validity claim. W151's paired and seed-level results need their endpoint definitions and observations before its statistical summaries can be reproduced. These dependencies are different; more citations do not resolve any of them. \autocite{W120,W150,W151}</data>
  <data key="d259">5f7b7ddb4b35b8c4cbce98705db7ec059791f00a6d5801bf01a3fc79035279f1</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["W120", "W150", "W151"]</data>
  <data key="d391">VERBATIM_BASELINE</data>
</node>
<node id="V10:TEXTREF:0230">
  <data key="d73">The source trail distinguishes the foundational software-engineering volume,
the two editions of the spec-driven work, the autonomous-agent volume and the
loop-</data>
  <data key="d74">cited_passage</data>
  <data key="d357">CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d358">V06</data>
  <data key="d355">appendices/series_practices.tex</data>
  <data key="d387">8</data>
  <data key="d388">15</data>
  <data key="d389">The source trail distinguishes the foundational software-engineering volume,
the two editions of the spec-driven work, the autonomous-agent volume and the
loop-engineering volume. \autocite{V01,V02,V03,V04,V05}
These references identify the author-supplied snapshots used here. Earlier
attributions inside them remain attached to the original occurrences in the
companion; this edition does not claim that the author invented every named
practice. Where a source's bibliography is incomplete, its unresolved key
remains unresolved rather than being turned into an inferred citation.</data>
  <data key="d259">22b38e75070777c30a123c52df25ddea11f65be347435d19dd7e4b66b9f7d61b</data>
  <data key="d183">CANONICAL_ID_AND_RECORDED_SCOPE_CHECKED_NOT_NEW_FULL_TEXT_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d390">["V01", "V02", "V03", "V04", "V05"]</data>
  <data key="d391">CHANGED_OR_NEW</data>
</node>
