<edge source="B022" target="P090" id="ND-fe66baba57b0981e">
  <data key="d420">ND_EDITORIAL_COMPARISON</data>
  <data key="d423">Proposizione del file: Le istruzioni persistenti rendono esplicite convenzioni, vincoli e decisioni del progetto. Confronto (static): Confrontare file di istruzioni, memoria esterna e responsabilità di aggiornamento; i meccanismi descritti non sono tutti equivalenti alla memoria virtuale gestita dal sistema. Scheda P090: An industry case describes Uber’s AI development platform, shared context, internal agents and review-related tooling.</data>
  <data key="d424">ND.zip; editorial file-level mapping, 2026-10-11</data>
  <data key="d428">AI_SW_ENG/chapters_verbose/chapter10/03_static_context.tex</data>
  <data key="d483">2</data>
  <data key="d467">EDITORIAL_NOT_EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d488">static</data>
  <data key="d489">Static Context Engineering: Teaching AI About Your Project (L2); Why Static Context Matters (L11); The AGENTS.md Pattern (L39)</data>
  <data key="d490">Frozen v6 node P090 summary/contribution and limitation</data>
  <data key="d491">Original publication March 10; updated March 11. Reported adoption percentages use different denominators. Author discloses former employment at Uber. The source’s correction distinguishes 84% agentic-tool adoption from 65–72% IDE code-generation figures and CLI-specific measures; those denominators must not be interchanged. An author correction in the March 12, 2026 Pulse distinguishes the IDE-generated-code share from an earlier erroneous percentage. Original date, updated text and company-level denominators remain separate. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d492">NO</data>
  <data key="d493">NO</data>
  <data key="d458">EDITORIAL_ARGUMENTED_UNSCORED</data>
