<edge source="B052" target="P085" id="ND-0e361f2cf3af8143">
  <data key="d420">ND_EDITORIAL_COMPARISON</data>
  <data key="d423">Proposizione del file: L’ecosistema viene organizzato in famiglie e scelte di progettazione. Confronto (adoption): Confrontare selezione degli strumenti, abilitazione del team e verifica degli esiti; una graduatoria o un piano di rollout non sostituisce un pilot controllato. Scheda P085: Interviews compare tool-selection practices across company sizes, including locally scored AI review trials and procurement constraints.</data>
  <data key="d424">ND.zip; editorial file-level mapping, 2026-10-11</data>
  <data key="d428">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter04_ecosystem.tex</data>
  <data key="d483">16</data>
  <data key="d467">EDITORIAL_NOT_EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d488">adoption</data>
  <data key="d489">Why the Ecosystem Fragmented (L16); The Four Must-Know Frameworks (L112); How to Read Part II (L196)</data>
  <data key="d490">Frozen v6 node P085 summary/contribution and limitation</data>
  <data key="d491">Company-local scoring exercises and tool selection are distinct from randomized productivity comparisons; evaluation samples and scoring scales are context-specific. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d492">NO</data>
  <data key="d493">NO</data>
  <data key="d458">EDITORIAL_ARGUMENTED_UNSCORED</data>
</edge>
