<edge source="B062" target="P086" id="ND-4048da2f6cc5409b">
  <data key="d420">ND_EDITORIAL_COMPARISON</data>
  <data key="d423">Proposizione del file: L’autonomia viene trattata come policy di esecuzione con budget ed escalation. Confronto (autonomy): Confrontare delega, arresto ed escalation. Le scale practitioner descrivono regimi di lavoro, non una misura validata e universale della maturità. Scheda P086: A written interview explores Yegge’s autonomy ladder, multi-agent work, fatigue and predictions about engineering employment.</data>
  <data key="d424">ND.zip; editorial file-level mapping, 2026-10-11</data>
  <data key="d428">AI_SDD_ENG_V2/chapters/chapter14_autonomy.tex</data>
  <data key="d483">642</data>
  <data key="d467">EDITORIAL_NOT_EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d488">autonomy</data>
  <data key="d489">The autonomy readiness checklist (L642); The Autonomy Spectrum: From Babysitting to Audit-After (L129); Autonomous-Guided (L199)</data>
  <data key="d490">Frozen v6 node P086 summary/contribution and limitation</data>
  <data key="d491">Yegge’s eight stages are a provocative practitioner ladder, not a validated maturity scale and not Osmani’s independent agency/orchestration axes. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d492">NO</data>
