<edge source="B085" target="P086" id="ND-7e523f3166b3e533">
  <data key="d420">ND_EDITORIAL_COMPARISON</data>
  <data key="d423">Proposizione del file: Lo sviluppo continuativo combina esecuzione autonoma, contesto rinnovato e una frontiera umana di approvazione. Confronto (autonomy): Confrontare delega, arresto ed escalation. Le scale practitioner descrivono regimi di lavoro, non una misura validata e universale della maturità. Scheda P086: A written interview explores Yegge’s autonomy ladder, multi-agent work, fatigue and predictions about engineering employment.</data>
  <data key="d424">ND.zip; editorial file-level mapping, 2026-10-11</data>
  <data key="d428">ai-auto_eng/AI_AUTO_ENG/chapters/chapter01_revolution.tex</data>
  <data key="d483">25</data>
  <data key="d467">EDITORIAL_NOT_EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION</data>
  <data key="d488">autonomy</data>
  <data key="d489">From Reactive to Proactive AI (L25); Prerequisites for Success (L246); What This Book Will Teach You (L319)</data>
  <data key="d490">Frozen v6 node P086 summary/contribution and limitation</data>
  <data key="d491">Yegge’s eight stages are a provocative practitioner ladder, not a validated maturity scale and not Osmani’s independent agency/orchestration axes. Subscriber-only article remainder not reviewed. No microdata replication, controlled product test, or independent-rater agreement study was performed.</data>
  <data key="d492">NO</data>
  <data key="d493">NO</data>
  <data key="d458">EDITORIAL_ARGUMENTED_UNSCORED</data>
</edge>
